hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"14401","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Janab, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution, lingering over it, and he said: O Abd Allah ibn Amr, six traits will come upon you. I said: What are they, may my father be ransom for you, O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom? He said: The seizure (death) of your Prophet — and it was as though my heart were torn out — say: One. So I said: One. He said: And the outpouring of wealth, until a thousand dinars comes to one of you and he still resents it; say: Two. So I said: Two. And a tribulation that enters the house of every man among you; say: Three. So I said: Three. And death like the sudden plague of sheep; say: Four. So I said: Four. And a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar (Romans); they will gather against you for the duration of a woman's pregnancy, and they will be readier to betray than you; say: Five. So I said: Five. And the conquest of the City; say: Six. So I said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, and which city? He said: Constantinople."
"14402","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in told me, Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, who said: I heard Ya'qub ibn Asim narrating that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will emerge among my nation and remain therein forty — I do not know whether he said: a day, or a month, or a year. Then Allah will send Isa, as though he were Urwah ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi; he will seek him and destroy him. Then the people will remain seven years with no enmity between any two. Then Allah will send a cold wind from the sky, and none in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of faith will remain except it will seize him."
"14403","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us. And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Yahya ibn al-Qimtah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, concerning His saying: We shall surely turn you to a qiblah that pleases you — he said: Toward the spout of the Ka'bah."
"14404","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Ya'la ibn Ata informed us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you permit me to wage jihad? He said: Do you have parents? He said: Yes. He said: Go and serve them well. So he went off, weaving through the riding camels."
"14405","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The pleasure of the Lord is in the pleasure of the father, and the wrath of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, is in the wrath of the father. And he did not raise it (to the Prophet)."
"14406","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Sulaym al-Sawwaf narrated to us, saying: The two Wasitis, Abu Bistam and Abu Mu'awiyah — meaning Shu'bah and Hushaym — bore witness, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pleasure of the Lord is in the pleasure of both parents, and the wrath of the Lord is in their wrath."
"14407","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, Sufyan and al-Hasan ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The killing of the believer is greater in Allah's sight than the passing of the world."
"14408","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and said: Allah is Greatest; praise be to Allah filling the heavens and the earth, and said things that Ata did not retain. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: Which of you spoke the words? The man said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I saw the angels vying, each outracing the other."
"14409","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar Sulayman ibn Hayyan informed us. And al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar informed us, from Hajjaj, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two men at the rear of the people in the Mosque of al-Khayf and ordered them to be brought; they were brought with their limbs trembling. He said: What kept you from praying with us? They said: We prayed in our dwellings. He said: Would you not pray with us so it counts as voluntary, while your first prayer is the obligatory one?! So al-Hajjaj narrated it from Ya'la ibn Ata, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he differed from the people in its chain. And Shu'bah, Abu Awanah, Hushaym, Ibrahim ibn Dhi Himayah, al-Thawri and Hisham ibn Hassan narrated it from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father."
"14410","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud narrated to us, Hisham ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi, from Abbad ibn Musa, from Muslim ibn Ri'ab, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am asking you about three things. He said: Ask whatever you wish. He said: How long will the people stand before the Lord of the worlds on the Day of Resurrection? And what of that standing is light upon the believer? And is there a station between Paradise and Hell? He said: As for your saying about the standing of the people before the Lord of the worlds on the Day of Resurrection: a thousand years in which they are not permitted (to speak). As for your saying: what of that standing is light upon the believer? The believers are two groups: as for the foremost, they are like two men conversing privately at length, then departing and entering Paradise. I said: How easy is this! Is there a station between Paradise and Hell? He said: Between them is my Basin; its parapets overlook Paradise, and its parapets extend over Hell; its length is a month and its width a month; whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; in it are cups of silver and flasks; whoever drinks a cup from it will find no thirst nor hunger until judgment is passed among the servants and he enters Paradise."
"14411","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Qur'an from four: from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."
"14412","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never obscene nor deliberately obscene, and he said: Among the most beloved of you to me are the best of you in character."
"14413","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr — I think he raised it — who said: Four traits, whoever has them in him is a pure hypocrite: when he speaks he lies, when he is entrusted he betrays, when he covenants he breaks faith, and when he disputes he acts wickedly; so whoever has one of them in him, in him is a trait of hypocrisy until he repents."
"14414","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa and Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith of al-Thawri."
"14415","Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four traits, whoever has them in him is a sheer hypocrite; and if one of them is in him, in him is a streak of hypocrisy until he abandons it: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his promise, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he disputes he acts wickedly."
"14416","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No sin harms along with Islam, just as no deed benefits along with polytheism."
"14417","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, no sin will harm him along with it, just as if he associated partners with Allah, no good deed would benefit him along with it. So Yahya ibn Yaman narrated it, and the people differed from him."
"14418","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, who said: A man — or an elder of the people of Madinah — came and stayed with Masruq, and said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said... and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Yahya ibn Yaman."
"14419","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, that he heard Ibrahim narrating from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Qur'an from four: Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, Mu'adh, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."
"14420","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It will be said to the companion of the Qur'an: Read and ascend, and recite as you used to recite in the world; for your station is at the last verse you recite."
"14421","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' and Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14422","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid and Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14423","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14424","Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn A'yan narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14425","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who emigrates from what Allah has forbidden."
"14426","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Amir al-Sha'bi told me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14427","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, Amir al-Sha'bi told me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14428","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, Bayan told me, from Amir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14429","Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muti' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sinan, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The emigrant is one who abandons evil, and the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"14430","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14431","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who emigrates from what Allah has forbidden."
"14432","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Hayyan informed us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, that three men entered upon Marwan ibn al-Hakam, and he told them that the first of the Signs to emerge is the Dajjal. They left him and entered upon Abd Allah ibn Amr, and informed him of Marwan's saying. He said: He has said nothing. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of the Signs to emerge is the rising of the sun from its west, and the Beast follows close upon it. Then he said: When the sun sets it comes beneath the Throne and prostrates, and it is said to it: Rise from where you used to rise. When that night comes, it seeks permission and is not answered; and when much of the night has passed, and the horizon is like a necklace, and it thinks that if it were permitted it would not reach (in time), it says: O Lord, how far is the east from the west! So it is said to it: Rise from where you set. And that is the saying of Allah, Majestic is His praise: Do they await but that the angels come to them, or your Lord comes, or some of your Lord's signs come — the verse."
"14433","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The grave sins are: associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents — or killing a soul, Shu'bah being the doubter — and the immersing oath."
"14434","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Harith, grandson of al-Sha'bi, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): In how long shall I read? He said: Read it in fourteen. I kept telling him I could do it in less than that, until he said: Read it in four. It never left me after that, and I wished I had accepted the concession."
"14435","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab narrated to us, Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ahwal told me, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gained spoils, he would order Bilal, who would call out among the people three times; the people would come with their spoils and he would divide them. Then a man came to him after that with a camel-halter of hair, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is what we had gained of the spoils. He said: Did you not hear Bilal calling three times? He said: Yes. He said: What kept you from bringing it? And he offered him an excuse. He said: You be the one to bring it on the Day of Resurrection; I will not accept it from you!"
"14436","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking; so none shall fast them."
"14437","Al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most wretched of people are three: the hamstringer of the she-camel of Thamud, and the son of Adam who killed his brother — no blood is shed on earth but some of it attaches to him, for he was the first to institute killing."
"14438","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd informed us. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sa'id al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"14439","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Safar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while we were building a dome, and said: The matter (the Hour) is swifter than that."
"14440","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Safar Sa'id ibn Yuhmid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while we were repairing a hut of ours, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? We said: A hut of ours that has weakened, and we are repairing it. He said: I see the matter (the Hour) is only more imminent than that."
"14441","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, from Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man on earth who says: There is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, but his sins are expiated, even if they were more than the foam of the sea."
"14442","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did not sin, Allah would create a creation who sin and then He forgives them."
"14443","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm and al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Raziyan narrated to us, both saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, from Layth, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever wishes to be moved away from the Fire and enter Paradise, let death come to him while he testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and let him love to come to people what he loves to be brought to him."
"14444","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi told me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to us, from his father, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient sin is it to withhold one's sustenance from those one maintains."
"14445","Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, both saying: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Harish ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Read the Qur'an in a month. I said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for me. He said: Read in three. I asked him for more, but he refused."
"14446","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Take the Qur'an from four: from Ibn Umm Abd, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."
"14447","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I shall never cease loving Ibn Mas'ud after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with him, saying: Take the Qur'an from four: from Ibn Umm Abd, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."
"14448","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, raising the hadith, who said: The likeness of one who sits on the bed of the absent woman is the likeness of one bitten by a black serpent of the black serpents of the Day of Resurrection."
"14449","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, saying: I heard al-A'mash — and al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab mentioned — from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, raising it, who said: Reviling the dead — and once he said: the dead (plural) — is like one on the verge of ruin."
"14450","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Safwan al-Ramli narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Hasan narrated to us. And Ibrahim ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not take knowledge by snatching it from the people; rather He takes the scholars, until when no scholar remains, the people take ignorant leaders; they are asked and give rulings without knowledge, so they stray and lead astray."
"14451","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ali ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Riqa' al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Fadl al-Qurashi of the offspring of Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer calls and some people establish the prayer, yet they are not believers."
"14452","Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari gave me a book, and I copied from it: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Aban ibn Taghlib narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make the hearers of His creation hear of him, and will belittle and humiliate him."
"14453","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: Allah has cursed wine, its presser, its drinker, its server, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, and the eater of its price."
"14454","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people performing ablution and saw their heels gleaming, and said: Woe to the heels from the Fire! Perfect the ablution."
"14455","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people performing ablution on a journey, and said: Perfect the ablution; woe to the heels from the Fire!"
"14456","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"14457","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying seated, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was told that you said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing — yet you are praying seated?! He said: Yes, but I am not like any of you."
"14458","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer seated is half the prayer. So I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying seated! I said: O Messenger of Allah, it reached me that you said: A man's prayer seated is half the prayer — yet you are praying seated?! He said: Yes, but I am not like any of you."
"14459","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Abu Iyad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast one day of every month and you have the reward of the rest; fast two days and you have the reward of the rest; fast three days and you have the reward of the rest; fast four days and you have the reward of the rest. He said: Then the fasting of the best fast is: fasting a day and breaking a day."
"14460","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Abu Iyad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, from Abu Iyad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr — raising it — who said: He forbade dubba', hantam and muzaffat (vessels). A Bedouin said: No vessels! He said: Drink, but avoid every intoxicant."
"14461","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jaban, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise: one disobedient to parents, a habitual drinker of wine, a reminder of favours, nor a child of adultery."
"14462","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father told me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jaban, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four shall not enter Paradise: the habitual drinker of wine, one disobedient to his parents, the child of adultery, and the reminder of favours."
"14463","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father told me, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Hani, that a man said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: Was Ali worthier, or Mu'awiyah? He said: No, rather Ali. I said: Then what brought you out? He said: Yet I neither struck with a sword nor shot an arrow; but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obey your father. So I obeyed him."
"14464","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The greatest sin in Allah's sight is for a man to neglect those he feeds."
"14465","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from an elder of al-Nakha', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I seek refuge in You from a soul that is never sated, a heart that does not humble itself, a supplication that is not heard, and knowledge that does not benefit; I seek refuge in You from these four."
"14466","Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk al-Mustamli narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muti' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from al-Aswad ibn Mas'ud, from Hanzalah ibn Khuwaylid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Ammar: The rebellious party will kill you."
"14467","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, from Abu al-Harr, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr — and I think he only raised it — saying: Whoever says every day a hundred times: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things Powerful — he is recorded as the best in deed of the people of that day, except one who says the like of what he said, or more."
"14468","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muslim al-A'war, from Habbah al-Urani, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The killer of Ammar and his despoiler are in the Fire."
"14469","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harun ibn Hatim narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise: one disobedient to parents, a reminder of favours, a habitual drinker of wine, nor a child of adultery."
"14470","Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya and Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you see those who lavish praise, throw dust in their faces."
"14471","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Ibn Abjar, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Beware these slaughter-places — meaning: the prayer-niches."
"14472","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir informed us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have completed the Qur'an; in how long shall I read it? He said: In a month. I said: I am able. He said: Then in twenty-five. I said: I am able. He said: Then in twenty. I said: I am able. He said: Then in fifteen. I said: I am able. He said: Then in five. I said: I am able. He said: No."
"14473","Bishr ibn Musa and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant falls ill, Allah says to His angels: Write for My servant what he used to do while free, until it appears to Me whether I take him or release him."
"14474","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father told me, Waki' narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abu Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14475","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us. And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim is afflicted with a trial in his body except that Allah commands the guardian angels who guard him, saying: Write for My servant every day and night the like of the good he used to do, so long as he remains confined in My bond."
"14476","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-A'yan Muhammad ibn Abi Attab narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father, saying: I heard al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah, who said: We sat with Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, when the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer in congregation. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed us, saying: Now then..."
"14477","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr narrating in the shade of the Ka'bah, saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; some of us were shooting arrows, some were in their grazing camp, and some were mending their tents, when it was called: Prayer in congregation. So we gathered to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed: No prophet before me but it was a duty to Allah upon him to guide his nation to what he knew was good for them and warn them of what he knew was evil for them. This nation has had its well-being placed in its first part, and its last part will be struck by trials, with tribulations following one upon another. A tribulation comes and one says: This will destroy me. Then it lifts, then another comes and one says: This will destroy me. Then it lifts. So whoever of you loves to be moved away from the Fire and enter Paradise, let death overtake him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him come to people what he loves to be brought to him. And whoever pledges an imam, giving him the clasp of his hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as much as he can. I said: This cousin of yours, Mu'awiyah, orders us to consume our wealth and shed our blood, though Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has said: O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among you unjustly — and said: And do not kill yourselves. He fell silent a while, then said: Obey him in obedience to Allah, and disobey him in disobedience to Allah."
"14478","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14479","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, both saying: Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar told me, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Rabb al-Ka'bah, who said: I saw a gathering at the House and inclined toward them, and there was a man narrating to them — and he was Abd Allah ibn Amr — saying: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and alighted at a station; some of us were building their tents, some were shooting arrows, and some were with their grazing livestock, when the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer in congregation. So I reached him and heard him say: No prophet was or is but upon him was to give his nation glad tidings of what he saw was good for them and warn them of what he saw was evil for them. Your nation's well-being is in its first part, and there will be trials and matters, each making the other seem light. The tribulation comes and one says: This. Then it lifts, then another comes and one says: This will destroy me. So whoever loves to be moved away from the Fire and enter Paradise, let him bring to people what he loves to be brought to him, and dislike what he dislikes to be brought to him. And whoever pledges an imam, giving him the clasp of his right hand and the fruit of his heart, let him obey him as much as he can; and if another man opposes him, cut off his head. I said, moving so — I parted between two men — and said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; my ears heard it and my heart retained it. I said: Then what do you command?! This cousin of yours, Mu'awiyah, orders us to kill ourselves and consume our wealth among us unjustly! So he placed his hand on his forehead, then raised it, and said: Go and obey him so long as he obeys Allah, and disobey him when he disobeys Allah."
"14480","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim al-Muflawaj narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware miserliness, for it destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever ties, so they severed; and to be miserly, so they were miserly; and to commit indecency, so they committed it."
"14481","Muhammad ibn Abi Zur'ah al-Dimashqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay' narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sulayman al-Nasri narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah al-Yashkuri, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, saying: Beware wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection; beware obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor deliberate obscenity; and beware avarice, for avarice destroyed those before you — it commanded them to sever their kinship ties, so they severed. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and which jihad is best? He said: That your blood be shed and your steed hamstrung. He said: Then which emigration is best? He said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes. And they are two emigrations: the emigration of the settled and the emigration of the Bedouin. As for the emigration of the Bedouin: when he is called he answers, and when he is commanded he obeys. As for the emigration of the settled: theirs is the severest trial and the greatest reward."
"14482","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Beware wrongdoing, for it is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection; beware obscenity, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not love the obscene, deliberately obscene one; and beware avarice, for it destroyed those before you — it commanded them to be miserly, so they were miserly; commanded them to commit indecency, so they committed it; and commanded them to sever kinship, so they severed. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best? He said: That the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand. Then that man — or another man — stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, which emigration is best? He said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes. Then he said: Emigration is two emigrations: the emigration of the settled and the emigration of the Bedouin. As for the emigration of the Bedouin: you answer him when he calls you and obey him when he commands you; and the settled one is greatest in trial and best in reward. And the wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid."
"14483","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said: Where are the poor of this nation and its destitute? So they will stand, and it will be said to them: What did you do? They will say: Our Lord, You tried us and we were patient, and You entrusted affairs and authority to others. Allah, Majestic is His remembrance, will say: You have spoken truly. So they will enter Paradise long before the people, while the severity of reckoning remains upon the wealthy and those in authority. They said: Then where are the believers that day? He said: Thrones of light will be set for them, with clouds shading them; that day will be shorter upon the believers than an hour of daytime."
"14484","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Talid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Zuhayr ibn al-Aqmar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that Mu'awiyah used to write in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14485","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: We were seated with Abu Ubaydah and they mentioned showing off. An elder surnamed Abu Yazid said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make the hearers of His creation hear of him, and will belittle and humiliate him."
"14486","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zanbur narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, an elder surnamed Abu Yazid told me, saying: I was seated with Abd Allah ibn Amr and Abd Allah ibn Umar, and Abd Allah ibn Umar said: Satan flows through the son of Adam like blood and spirit. So Abd Allah ibn Amr wept and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make the hearers of His creation hear of him, and will belittle and humiliate him."
"14487","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, all saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard a man in the house of Abu Ubaydah narrating that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr narrating to Abd Allah ibn Umar that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make the hearers of His creation hear of him, and will belittle and humiliate him. So the eyes of Abd Allah ibn Umar shed tears."
"14488","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, who said: The Signs were mentioned in the presence of Marwan, and they mentioned the Dajjal. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The swiftest of the Signs are: the rising of the sun from its west, or the emergence of the Beast upon the people in the forenoon; whichever of them comes before the other, the other follows close upon it. Then Abd Allah ibn Amr said: So I think the rising of the sun is the first of them."
"14489","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Amr ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, both saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard Sayf narrating from Rushayd al-Hajari, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"14490","Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Hilal al-Hajari, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden."
"14491","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir al-Khaywani, who said: I came to Bayt al-Maqdis and sat with Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sufficient sin for a man is to neglect those he feeds."
"14492","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir al-Khaywani, who said: I was with Abd Allah ibn Amr, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sufficient sin is it for a man to neglect those he feeds."
"14493","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sufficient sin for a man is to neglect those he feeds."
"14494","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ya'juj and Ma'juj are of the offspring of Adam; if they were released they would corrupt the people's livelihoods; none of them dies without leaving a thousand or more of his progeny; and beyond them are three nations: Tawil, Taris and Mansak."
"14495","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar al-Muqa'ad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me and called me, saying: In how long do you read the Qur'an? I said: In two days and two nights. He said: Bravo! Pray and sleep, sleep and pray; read in a month. I said: I am stronger than that. So he reduced with me and I bargained with him until it reached seven. He said: How do you fast? I said: I fast and do not break. He said: Fast and break; fast three days of every month. I said: I am stronger than that. So he reduced with me and I bargained with him. He said: If you refuse, then fast the most beloved fast to Allah, the fast of Dawud: fast a day and break a day. For my accepting the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is dearer to me than my family and my wealth."
"14496","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14497","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How shall I read the Qur'an? He said: In seven nights. He said: I kept bargaining with him, until he said: Read it in a day and a night; do not exceed that."
"14498","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: It has reached me about you that you fast and do not break, and pray and do not sleep. He said: Fast three days of every month, and read the Qur'an in two months. So he reduced with me and I bargained with him, and he kept reducing with me, until he said: Fast a day and break a day, and read the Qur'an in seven."
"14499","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that some Jews greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), having said to themselves: Why does Allah not punish us for what we say. So it was revealed: And when they come to you, they greet you with what Allah does not greet you with."
"14500","Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Death be upon you. And they said to themselves: Why does Allah not punish us for what we say. So Allah revealed: And when they come to you, they greet you with what Allah does not greet you with — the whole verse."
"14501","14463 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib: my father informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared Fatimah for her marriage to Ali, he sent with her a khamil. Ata said: What is a khamil? He said: A velvet cloth (qatifah), a leather pillow stuffed with palm fiber or idhkhir grass, and a waterskin; they would spread half of the khamil beneath them and cover themselves with its other half."
"14502","14464 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he instructed Ali and Fatimah, when they took to their beds, to say Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah), Allahu Akbar (Allah is Greatest), and Alhamdulillah (praise be to Allah), thirty-three times, thirty-three times, and thirty-four times."
"14503","14465 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad alone. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have excluded a great many people!"
"14504","14466 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man said in prayer: Allah is Greatest; praise be to Allah, filling the heavens and filling the earth. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who is the one who spoke those words? A man said: I did. So he said: I saw the angels receiving them, each of them hastening ahead of the other."
"14505","14467 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prostration, and said at the end of his prostration: Uff, uff! Did You not promise me that You would not punish them while they seek forgiveness?!"
"14506","14468 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The sun eclipsed ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"14507","14469 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs during the eclipse of the sun."
"14508","14470 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The sun eclipsed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer ... then he mentioned something similar."
"14509","14471 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The sun eclipsed in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prolonged the standing ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"14510","14472 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship the Most Merciful, spread peace, and feed food; you will enter the Gardens."
"14511","14473 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"14512","14474 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until seventy liars come forth."
"14513","14475 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man in the pre-Islamic age of ignorance walked strutting arrogantly in a fine suit of clothes, letting his lower garment trail; so Allah commanded the earth, and it seized him, and he keeps sinking and tumbling in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"14514","14476 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man from among those before you went out in a fine suit of clothes, strutting proudly in it; so Allah commanded the earth, and it seized him, and he keeps sinking within it until the Day of Resurrection."
"14515","14477 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"14516","14478 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"14517","14479 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaniyy narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Among the Children of Israel there was a young goat among abundant sheep, whose mother would suckle it; then it broke loose and suckled all the sheep, yet it was still not satisfied. That reached their prophet, so he said: The likeness of this is the likeness of a people who will come after you: a man among them will be given enough to suffice a tribe or a nation, yet he will not be satisfied."
"14518","14480 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaniyy narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A guest stayed among the Children of Israel with some people, and they had a pregnant bitch; she said: I will not bark at my family's guest tonight, but the puppies in her belly howled. In the morning they went to a prophet of theirs and told him, and he said: Do you know what the likeness of this is? They said: No. He said: The likeness of a nation that will come after you, whose foolish ones will overpower its wise ones."
"14519","14481 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"14520","14482 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, accept my pledge, for I have left my parents weeping. He said: Go back and make them laugh as you made them weep, and he refused to accept his pledge."
"14521","14483 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have come to pledge to you upon emigration, and I left my parents weeping. He said: Go back to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"14522","14484 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him upon emigration, and said: I left my parents weeping and have come to you to pledge to you. He said: Go back to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"14523","14485 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging him upon emigration, having left his parents weeping. He said: Go back to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"14524","14486 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Tarif, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting the verses in prayer."
"14525","14487 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from al-Fadl ibn Salih, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw dust in the faces of those who praise excessively."
"14526","14488 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abbad, from al-Fadl ibn Salih, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: After me there will be tribulations in which the Arabs will be uprooted; the tongue therein will be sharper than the sword, and all its slain will be in the Fire."
"14527","14489 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us - both said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two qualities ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"14528","14490 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are two qualities which no Muslim man preserves except that he enters Paradise; they are easy, yet few act upon them ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"14529","14491 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two qualities ... then he mentioned the same."
"14530","14492 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Babah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when deeds were mentioned, and he said: There are no days in which deeds are more excellent than in these ten days. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad? He deemed it great and said: Not even jihad, except for a man who goes out with his life and his wealth, then his very lifeblood is spent therein."
"14531","14493 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn Babah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was praying seated, and said: Indeed, the one praying seated has half the prayer of the one standing."
"14532","14494 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Qutbah ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn Babi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was praying seated, and said: The prayer of the seated one is half the prayer of the standing one."
"14533","14495 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a soul that is never satisfied, from knowledge that does not benefit, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a supplication that is not heard. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of these four."
"14534","14496 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Dawud al-Hamdani, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me and said: Shall I not teach you some words? Whoever Allah intends good for, He teaches them to him?! I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, I am weak, so take my forelock toward good, and make Islam the utmost limit of my contentment. O Allah, I am weak, so strengthen my weakness in what pleases You; I am lowly, so honor me; and I am poor, so enrich me."
"14535","14497 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Musa, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The prayer of the seated one is half the prayer of the standing one."
"14536","14498 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Musa, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The prayer of the seated one is half the prayer of the standing one."
"14537","14499 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Bashir Abu Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ride the sea except as a pilgrim performing Hajj, or one performing Umrah, or a warrior in the path of Allah; for beneath the sea there is fire, and beneath the fire there is sea. And do not buy anything from one under coercion by a ruler."
"14538","14500 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, that Nawf and Abd Allah ibn Amr met, and Nawf said: I find in the Torah that if the heavens and the earth and all within them were a single plate of iron, and a man said: There is no god but Allah, it would pierce through them until it reached Allah. Abd Allah said: And I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We prayed Isha with him one night; some went back and some remained behind, then he came before the people had dispersed from Isha prayer, breathing heavily, having counted twenty and pointing with the forefinger, saying: Your Lord Almighty has opened a door from the doors of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, and adding: These are My servants; they have fulfilled one obligation and await another."
"14539","14501 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from Nawf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, the same as above."
"14540","14502 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Mutarrif, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib; some remained behind and some returned, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: This is your Lord; He has opened a door from the doors of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: My servants have fulfilled one obligation and await another."
"14541","14503 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shubah and Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reads the Quran in less than three days has not understood it."
"14542","14504 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Ibn Abi Rabiah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I mentioned fasting to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Fast one day out of every ten days, and for you is the reward of the nine. I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Then fast one day out of every nine days, and for you is the reward of the eight. I said: I am stronger than that. He said: Then fast one day out of every eight days, and for you is the reward of the seven. I said: I am stronger than that. He kept on until he said: Fast one day and break fast one day."
"14543","14505 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would speak to us most of the night, not standing except for the weighty prayer."
"14544","14506 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad, the freedman of Banu Hashim, who was among the companions of Makhul, from Salih ibn Jubayr, from Abu al-Ajfa, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the Quran from four: from Ibn Umm Abd, and Muadh, and Ubayy, and Salim. I had intended to send them to the nations as Isa sent the disciples from among the Children of Israel. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, why not Abu Bakr and Umar? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no being without them; their likeness in religion is like that of hearing and sight."
"14545","14507 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Abu Sabrah: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah Almighty hates the obscene and the deliberately obscene one. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour will not come until obscenity and deliberate obscenity appear, and bad neighborliness, and severing of kinship, and until the trustworthy is deemed treacherous and the treacherous is deemed trustworthy. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the most sound in Islam among Muslims is the one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe, and the best emigration is emigration from what Allah has forbidden. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the likeness of the believer is like that of the bee: it eats wholesome and produces wholesome, and when it lands it neither breaks nor spoils. Indeed I have a Basin, between its two sides is like what is between Ayla and Makkah - or he said: Sanaa and Madinah - and in it are pitchers like the stars; it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; whoever drinks from it will never thirst thereafter."
"14546","14508 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us. And Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Abu Sabrah: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty hates the obscene, deliberately obscene one. The Hour will not come until obscenity and deliberate obscenity appear, and bad neighborliness and severing of kinship, and until the treacherous is deemed trustworthy and the trustworthy is deemed treacherous. Indeed your appointed meeting is my Basin: its length and width are one, like what is between Ayla and Makkah, a month's journey; in it are pitchers like the stars; its drink is whiter than silver; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst thereafter."
"14547","14509 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Tamam narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Bishr ibn Shighaf, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing more honored to Allah - Majestic His remembrance - on the Day of Resurrection than the son of Adam. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, not even the angels? He said: Not even the angels; the angels are compelled, at the rank of the sun and the moon."
"14548","14510 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Aslam al-Ijli, from Bishr ibn Shighaf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Sur? He said: It is a horn that will be blown into."
"14549","14511 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Aslam al-Ijli, from Bishr ibn Shighaf, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Sur? He said: A horn that will be blown into."
"14550","14512 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Suwayd ibn Hujayr, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, who said: A man asked Abd Allah ibn Amr: Which of the believers is best in Islam? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe. He said: Then which of the believers is best in faith? He said: The best of them in character. He said: Then which of the emigrants is best? He said: The one who emigrates from what Allah has forbidden. He said: Then which jihad is best? He said: The one who strives against his own self for Allah. He said: Did you say this, O Abd Allah ibn Amr, or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14551","14513 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Umar ibn Sayf, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A fire will be raised upon the people of the east and will gather them to the west; it will spend the night with them wherever they spend the night, and rest at midday with them wherever they rest; it will take whoever falls behind and lags from them, driving them as a lame camel is driven."
"14552","14514 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in a dream that they took the pillar of the Book and carried it to Sham; so when tribulations occur, safety is in Sham."
"14553","14515 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us. And al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Aqil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Said ibn Mina, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who fasts continuously; shall I fast the fast of a lifetime? He said: No. I said: Shall I fast two days and break one day? He said: No. I kept reducing it with him, and he said: Fast the fast of Dawud (peace be upon him), for he would fast one day and break fast one day."
"14554","14516 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Awf, from Maymun ibn Ustadh al-Hazzani, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation wears gold and dies wearing it, Allah will forbid him the gold of Paradise; and whoever of my nation dies wearing silk, Allah will forbid him the silk of Paradise."
"14555","14517 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Maymun ibn Ustadh, from al-Sadafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation dies adorned with gold, Allah will forbid him its adornment in the Hereafter; and whoever of my nation dies drinking wine, Allah will forbid him its drink in the Hereafter; and whoever of my nation dies wearing silk, he will be denied wearing it in the Hereafter."
"14556","14518 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Abu Umamah al-Thaqafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb (kinship) will be set up on the Day of Resurrection, having a hook like the hook of the spindle; it will speak with fluent, eloquent tongues, joining whoever joined it and severing whoever severed it."
"14557","14519 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, who said: Abd Allah ibn Rabah wrote to me, and narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we sat at the door; he heard two men differing over a verse, so he came out to us with anger visible in his face and said: Those before you perished only because of their frequent disputing about the Quran."
"14558","14520 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash: Uthman ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither the green sky has shaded nor the dusty earth has carried a man more truthful than Abu Dharr."
"14559","14521 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither the dusty earth has carried nor the green sky has shaded one with a dialect more truthful than Abu Dharr."
"14560","14522 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Azhar ibn al-Qasim informed us. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Azhar ibn al-Qasim al-Rasibi narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Babi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Allah boasts to His angels on the evening of Arafah about the people of Arafah, saying: Look at My servants; they have come to Me disheveled and dusty."
"14561","14523 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: Nawf al-Bikali and Abd Allah ibn Amr met, and Nawf said: If the heavens and the earth were placed in one pan of the scale and There is no god but Allah in another pan, There is no god but Allah would outweigh them; and if the heavens and the earth were a plate of iron, There is no god but Allah would pierce through them. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Maghrib prayer; some remained behind and some left, then he came out when half the night had passed, having uncovered his knees in alarm, breathing heavily, saying: Rejoice, O company of Muslims! Rejoice! This is your Lord; He has opened a door of heaven, boasting of you to the angels, saying: Look at My servants; they have fulfilled one obligation and await another."
"14562","14524 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, both said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer times. He said: The time of Zuhr prayer is when the sun declines, so that a man's shadow is like his height, as long as Asr has not come; the time of Asr is as long as the sun has not set; the time of Maghrib is as long as the twilight has not disappeared; the time of Isha is until half the night; and the time of Fajr is from the rising of dawn as long as the sun has not risen. This Abu Ayyub from whom Qatadah narrated is al-Azdi; his name is Yahya ibn Malik, trustworthy."
"14563","14525 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah - I think it is Ibn Amr - Shubah said: Sometimes he would raise it (to the Prophet) and sometimes he would not raise it - he said: The time of Asr is as long as the time of Maghrib has not come; the time of Maghrib is as long as the twilight has not fallen; the time of Isha is as long as half the night has not passed; and the time of Subh is as long as the sun has not risen."
"14564","14526 - Abu al-Darda Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath al-Antartusi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Shubah, from Qatadah ibn Diamah, from Abu Ayyub al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The first prayer is before the time of Asr enters; Asr is before the sun turns yellow; Maghrib is before the twilight falls; the last Isha is at half the night; and Subh is before the sun rises."
"14565","14527 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The chief sweet basil of the people of Paradise is henna."
"14566","14528 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Susi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wished to sleep while in a state of major impurity would perform ablution."
"14567","14529 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Susi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, the same as above."
"14568","14530 - Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah, from Uqbah ibn Aws al-Sadusi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the day of the Conquest and magnified Allah three times, then said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone. Indeed every inherited honor from the pre-Islamic age that is mentioned and claimed, and every blood and wealth, is beneath these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the House and the watering of the pilgrims. Indeed the slain of mistaken killing resembling the intentional, by whip or stick, is one hundred camels, among them forty pregnant with their young."
"14569","14531 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Qasim ibn Rabiah, from Uqbah ibn Aws al-Sadusi, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, he said: There is no god but Allah alone; He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone ... then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd."
"14570","14532 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Rabiah narrating from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The killing of mistake resembling the intentional, the slain of the whip and the stick, entails one hundred camels, among them forty pregnant with their young."
"14571","14533 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Uqbah ibn Wassaj, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a watering vessel of gold ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"14572","14534 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an enclosure of the enclosures of Madinah, when a man came and sought permission. He said: Stand and permit him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I stood and permitted him, and behold it was Abu Bakr, so I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he kept praising Allah until he sat. Then a man came and sought permission, and he said: Stand and permit him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I stood and permitted him, and behold it was Umar, so I gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he kept praising Allah until he sat. Then one came in a low voice, and he said: Stand and permit him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise upon a trial that will befall him. So I stood and permitted him, and behold it was Uthman, so I gave him glad tidings of Paradise upon a trial that would befall him, and he kept saying: O Allah, patience, until he sat. I said: O Messenger of Allah, where am I? He said: You are with your father."
"14573","14535 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Hanafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"14574","14536 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Hanafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an enclosure when a man came and sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... then he mentioned the same."
"14575","14537 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man sought permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He entered, and behold it was Abu Bakr. Then a man sought permission, and he said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He entered, and behold it was Umar ibn al-Khattab. And a man sought permission, and he said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Uthman ibn Affan entered. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: Where am I, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You are with your father."
"14576","14538 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Salim al-Khayyat narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: After me there will be rulers who will delay prayer from its times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what should one who lives to see them do? He said: Pray it at its time; then when you attend prayer with them, pray."
"14577","14539 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him - he said it three times - and if he drinks it a fourth time, kill him."
"14578","14540 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People will emerge from the east reciting the Quran, yet it will not pass their throats; every time one generation is cut off, another generation arises, until the Dajjal will be with their remnant."
"14579","14541 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us. And Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, both said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Asid, from Raja ibn Haywah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A little understanding is better than much worship; it suffices a man in understanding when he worships Allah, and it suffices a man in ignorance when he is pleased with his own opinion. People are but two men: a believer and an ignorant one; so do not harm the believer, and do not dispute with the ignorant."
"14580","14542 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be among you a people who recite the Quran, yet it will not pass their heads; every time a generation rises among them it is cut off, every time a generation rises among them it is cut off - until he mentioned twenty times and more - until the last of them will emerge with the Dajjal."
"14581","From Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Emigration after emigration, until people emigrate to the emigration place of Ibrahim, and none remains on earth except the worst of its people; the spirit of Allah will deem them foul and their land will cast them out, and the Fire will gather them from Aden with the apes and the pigs; it will spend the night with them wherever they spend the night, and rest at midday with them wherever they rest, and it will take whoever falls behind from them."
"14582","14543 - Ismail ibn Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a carrier of understanding is not understanding; whoever is not benefited by his knowledge, his ignorance harms him. Read the Quran as long as it restrains you; if it does not restrain you, then you are not truly reading it."
"14583","14544 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, from Makhul, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he finished he said to us: Do you recite the Quran when you are with me in prayer? We said: Yes. He said: Then do not do so, except with the Mother of the Quran."
"14584","14545 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri and Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: While I was asleep I saw the pillar of the Book lifted from beneath my head; I followed it with my sight, and behold it had been carried to Sham. Indeed faith, when tribulations come, is in Sham - three times."
"14585","14546 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah al-Saluli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Convey from me even a verse, and narrate from the Children of Israel without harm; and whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"14586","14547 - Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah al-Saluli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Forty good deeds, the highest of them the lending of a goat; whoever performs one of them hoping for its reward, Allah will admit him to Paradise."
"14587","14548 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Kabshah al-Saluli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright and moderate; the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer."
"14588","14549 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine, Allah will not accept prayer from him for forty days."
"14589","14550 - Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us. And Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated to us, both said: al-Awzai narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, Allah will not accept his repentance for forty mornings; if he repents, Allah will turn to him; if he returns, He will not accept his repentance for forty mornings; if he repents, Allah will turn to him - three or four times. Al-Awzai said: I do not know whether in the third or in the fourth: If he returns, it will be binding upon Allah Almighty to give him to drink from the discharge of al-Khabal on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Awzai said: The discharge of al-Khabal is the pus of the people of the Fire."
"14590","14551 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... the like of the hadith of al-Awzai."
"14591","14552 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamadhani narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Abu Sallam al-Habashi, from Ibn al-Daylami, who said: I came to Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drinks wine is impure, and his prayer is impure for forty days; if he repents, Allah will turn to him; then if he returns, he is impure and his prayer is impure for forty days; then if he repents, Allah will turn to him; then if he returns, he is impure and his prayer is impure for forty days; and if he repents, Allah will turn to him; but if he returns, it will be binding upon Allah to give him to drink from the discharge of al-Khabal on the Day of Resurrection."
"14592","14553 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sulayman ibn Dawud asked Allah for three things, and Allah gave him two; and I hope He gave him the third: he asked Him to judge with a judgment coinciding with His judgment, and he was given it; he asked Him for a kingdom befitting none after him, and he was given it; and he asked that any servant who comes to Bayt al-Maqdis, intending only prayer therein, emerge from his sin as on the day his mother bore him."
"14593","14554 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sulayman ibn Dawud asked his Lord for three things, and He gave him two; and I hope He has given him the third: he asked his Lord for a judgment coinciding with His judgment, and He gave him; he asked Him for a kingdom befitting none after him, and He gave him; and he asked that any man who leaves his house intending only prayer in this mosque - meaning the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis - emerge from his sin as on the day his mother bore him; and we hope He has given him that."
"14594","14555 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sulayman ibn Dawud asked Allah Almighty for three things: he asked Him for a kingdom befitting none after him, and He gave it to him; he asked Him for a judgment coinciding with His judgment, and He gave him; and he asked that whoever comes to this House, intending only prayer therein, be forgiven."
"14595","14556 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Sibani, from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah created His creation in darkness, and cast upon them from His light; whoever is touched by that light is guided, and whoever misses it goes astray. Therefore I say: The pen has dried upon the knowledge of Allah."
"14596","14557 - Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Daylami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah created His creation in darkness, then cast upon them from His light; whoever is touched by that light is guided, and whoever misses it goes astray. Therefore I say: The pen has dried upon the knowledge of Allah."
"14597","14558 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us. And Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, Thawabah ibn Awn Abu Awn al-Tanukhi narrated to us, who said: I heard Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me awake; and whoever sees me has seen the truth, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"14598","14559 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi, who said: I was with my father at Huwwarayn when I was a young lad, and I saw people gathered around a man. I said: Who is this? They said: Abd Allah ibn Amr. I heard him narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Among the signs of the Hour's nearness: the wicked will be raised and the good lowered; speech will be set loose and action restrained; and the mathnah will be read among the people. It was said: What is the mathnah? He said: Whatever is written besides the Book of Allah."
"14599","14560 - Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Shurahbil ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Shufah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a dyed garment on me and said: What is this? So I went and burnt it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you do with your garment? I said: I burnt it. He said: Why did you not clothe some of your women with it?!"
"14600","14561 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw the pillar of the Book taken from beneath my pillow; I followed it with my sight, and behold it was a radiant light toward Sham."
"14601","14562 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Muhannad ibn Khalid al-Tamimi narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn Rafi al-Hadrami, from al-Hanan ibn Kharijah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about emigration. He said: When you establish prayer, give zakat, and abandon obscenities, outward and inward, then you are an emigrant even if you die in settled land. Then a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about the garments of the people of Paradise: are they created by creation or woven by weaving? He said: Rather the fruits of Paradise will split open with them."
"14602","14563 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: Harami ibn Hafs al-Qasmali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd Allah narrated to us that al-Hanan ibn Kharijah narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: While we were around the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about the garments of Paradise: a creation created, or a weaving woven? Some of the people laughed, and he said: Why do you laugh? That an ignorant one asks a learned one?! He sat a little, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is the asker about the garments of Paradise?! He said: Here he is, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No; rather the fruit of Paradise will be split open with them - he said it three times."
"14603","14564 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamadhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to me, from al-Abbas ibn Salim, from Mudrik ibn Abd Allah al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith, when tribulations occur, is in Sham - three times."
"14604","14565 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabairi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Jumahi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Successful is he who submits and whose provision is sufficient."
"14605","14566 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Jumahi said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated a hadith to me and I wrote it; when I had memorized it, I erased it. He said: Successful is he who submits and whose provision is sufficient, and who is patient upon that."
"14606","14567 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us. And Salamah ibn Nahid al-Maqdisi and Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, both said: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us: Umar ibn Yazid al-Nasri narrated to me, Amr ibn Muhajir narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from Yahya ibn al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No nation ever perished except through the rain-stars (belief in stellar causation), and the beginning of its polytheism was only denial of the Decree."
"14607","14568 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Yaman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him - he said it three times - and if he returns a fourth time, kill him."
"14608","14569 - Said ibn Abduwayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Dabbi narrated to us, Nuh ibn Darraj narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The affair of the Children of Israel remained close-knit until there grew among them the offspring of the captives of the nations whom the Children of Israel used to take captive; then they spoke by their own opinion, and went astray and led astray."
"14609","14570 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us. And Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shuayb ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen eating reclining, nor with two men treading upon his heels."
"14610","14571 - Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Shuayb ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast one day and for you are ten. I said: Give me more. He said: Fast two days and for you are nine. I said: Give me more. He said: Fast three days and for you are eight. Thabit said: I mentioned that to Mutarrif, and he said: I see only that he increased in action and decreased in reward."
"14611","14572 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: While I sat in the mosque in a circle of the poor Emigrants, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and sat with them; so I stood toward them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the poor Emigrants rejoice at what gladdens their faces; for they will enter Paradise forty autumns (years) before the rich. I saw their faces brighten, until I wished I were among them."
"14612","14573 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Kab ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask al-Wasilah for me; for it is a station in Paradise befitting only one servant among the servants of Allah, and I hope I am he. Whoever asks al-Wasilah for me, intercession becomes due for him."
"14613","14574 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. Ishaq said: And Waki informed us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two saffron-dyed garments on me and said: Cast them off, for they are among the garments of the people of the Fire. So I cast them off."
"14614","14575 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus and Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Rafi, from Ismail ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Muhajir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever reads the Quran, it is as if prophethood has been enfolded between his sides, except that no revelation comes to him. Whoever reads the Quran and sees that anyone has been given better than what he has been given has magnified what Allah deemed small and diminished what Allah deemed great. It does not befit the bearer of the Quran to be foolish among the foolish, nor to anger among the angry, nor to rage among those who rage; rather he pardons and overlooks, by virtue of the Quran."
"14615","14576 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever withholds surplus water or pasture, Allah will withhold His bounty from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"14616","14577 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar Rustah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muhasir ibn Habib, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seek refuge from the evil of the four: from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard. And he said: Whoever sends blessings upon me, Allah sends blessings upon him tenfold."
"14617","14578 - Muhammad ibn al-Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamadhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to me, from al-Abbas ibn Salim, from Mudrik ibn Abd Allah al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith, when tribulations occur, is in Sham - three times."
"14618","14579 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, from Hariz ibn Uthman, from Hayyan ibn Zayd al-Sharabi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Show mercy and you will be shown mercy. Woe to the funnels of speech! Woe to those who persist in what they did while they know!"
"14619","14580 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muslim ibn Jubayr, from Abu Sufyan, from Amr ibn Harish, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to prepare an army, and the camels ran out. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the camels have run out. He said: Take from the young camels of charity. So I took one camel for two, against the charity camels."
"14620","14581 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati and Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, both said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Hajj for one who has not performed Hajj is better than ten campaigns; a campaign for one who has performed Hajj is better than ten Hajjes; a campaign at sea is better than ten campaigns on land; whoever crosses the sea, it is as if he has crossed all the valleys; and the seasick therein is like one weltering in his blood."
"14621","14582 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to me, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Ansari narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever harms the people of Madinah, Allah will harm him; upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him."
"14622","14583 - Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, from Hilal ibn Abi Hilal, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: This verse in the Quran - O Prophet, We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, and a warner - is in the Torah: O Prophet, We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, a warner, and a refuge for the unlettered; you are My servant and My Messenger; I have named you al-Mutawakkil; you are neither harsh nor rude, nor clamorous in the markets; you do not repel evil with evil, but pardon and overlook. I will not take you until I straighten through you the crooked creed, opening through you blind eyes, deaf ears, and covered hearts, so that they say: There is no god but Allah. And this verse in the Quran - O you who believe, wine, gambling, idols, and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may prosper - is in the Torah: Allah Almighty sent down the truth to remove falsehood thereby, and to abolish thereby play, grand Satanic deceptions, flutes, stringed instruments, pipes, poetry, and wine. My Lord swore by an oath: No servant shall drink it after I have forbidden it except that I shall make him thirsty on the Day of Resurrection; and none shall abandon it after I have forbidden it except that I shall give him to drink from the enclosure of sanctity."
"14623","14584 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid al-Massisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The angels said: Our Lord, You gave the children of Adam the world, wherein they eat, drink, and wear clothes, while we glorify You with praise and neither eat nor drink nor amuse ourselves; just as You made the world for them, make the Hereafter for us. He said: I shall not make the righteous offspring of one whom I created with My Hands like one to whom I said: Be, and he was."
"14624","14585 - Abu Zurah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, who said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Saqab, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man of the desert folk came to him wearing a cloak of sijan cloth buttoned with brocade. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intends to raise every shepherd son of a shepherd and lower every horseman son of a horseman. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the folds of his cloak and said: Do I not see upon him the clothing of one who has no sense. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When death came to the Prophet of Allah Nuh, he said to his son: O my son, I counsel you, and I shall make the counsel brief: I command you with two things and forbid you two things: I command you with There is no god but Allah, for if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed in one pan and There is no god but Allah in a pan, it would outweigh them; and if the seven heavens and the seven earths were a closed ring, There is no god but Allah would shatter them. And I counsel you with Glory be to Allah and with His praise, for it is the prayer of creation, and through it creation is provided for. And I forbid you disbelief and arrogance. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, disbelief we know; what is arrogance? Is it for a man to have two fine sandals with fine straps, which pleases him? He said: No. He said: Is it for him to have a fine suit which he wears? He said: No. He said: Is it for him to have a beautiful horse whose beauty pleases him? He said: No. He said: Is it for one of us to have companions who sit with him? He said: No. He said: Then what is arrogance? He said: To belittle the truth and despise people."
"14625","14586 - Rayhan ibn Yazid: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri (H). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, who said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, who said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Rayhan ibn Yazid al-Amiri, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich one, nor for one possessing strength and vigor."
"14626","14587 - Al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, who said: Abu Musab narrated to us (H). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, who said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us (H). And al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, who said: Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Madini narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Muslim ibn al-Walid ibn Rabah, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: I swear not, I swear not, I swear not, then he descended and said: Rejoice! Rejoice! Whoever prays the five prayers and avoids the major sins will enter through whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes. Al-Muttalib said: I heard a man asking Abd Allah ibn Amr: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention them? He said: Yes: disobedience to parents, associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, slandering chaste women, consuming the wealth of the orphan, fleeing from the battle line, and consuming usury."
"14627","14588 - Chapter: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, who said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, who said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab Abu al-Ala, who said: Ikrimah narrated to me, who said: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to me, who said: While we were around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when tribulation was mentioned, or was mentioned in his presence, he said: When you see that people's pledges are corrupted and their trusts diminished, and they become like this - and he interlaced his fingers - I stood toward him and said: What should I do then, may Allah make me your ransom? He said: Stay in your house, restrain your tongue, take what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to the affair of the elite, and leave the affair of the commonfolk."
"14628","14589 - Umarah ibn Amr ibn Hazm: Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Umarah ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What will become of you in a time - or a time is about to come - in which people will be sifted as grain is sifted, and there will remain the dregs of people whose pledges and trusts are corrupted; they will differ and become like this - and he interlaced his fingers. They said: What of us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you know, leave what you disapprove, turn to the affair of your own elite, and leave the affair of your commonfolk."
"14629","14590 - Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban: Musa ibn Jumhur al-Simsar al-Tinnisi narrated to us, who said: Duhaym narrated to us, who said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, who said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As informed him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What will become of you when a time comes in which people are sifted as grain, and you remain among the dregs of people whose pledges are corrupted and who neglect their trusts, and they become like this - and he put his fingers into one another. They said: What should we do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to your own elite, and leave their commonfolk."
"14630","14591 - Ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Umarah ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as above."
"14631","14592 - Uqbah ibn Aws: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, who said: Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us, who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Uqbah ibn Aws, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people whose pledges and trusts are corrupted, whose necks differ, and they become like this - and he crossed his fingers - He said: How is the escape, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to your private self, and beware their commonfolk."
"14632","14593 - Al-Hasan: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Man narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: How will you be when you are among the dregs of people whose pledges and trusts are corrupted, and they differ and become like this? Then he put his fingers into one another. I said: What for me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to your elite, and beware their commonfolk."
"14633","14594 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Subayh, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people ... then he mentioned the hadith."
"14634","14595 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, who said: Mamar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, who said: Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, who said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from [...], from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when you are among the dregs of people whose pledges are corrupted, whose trusts are corrupted, and whose hearts differ?! And he interlaced his fingers. He said: What should I do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Attend to what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to your private self, and beware their commonfolk."
"14635","14596 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, who said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dinar al-Nili, from al-Hasan: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people whose hearts and trusts are corrupted, and whose hearts differ?! And he interlaced his fingers. He said: What should I do? He said: Attend to what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to your private self, and beware their commonfolk."
"14636","14597 - Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah and Ahmad ibn Mabahrâm al-Idhaji narrated to us, both said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, who said: Nuh ibn Qays informed us, who said: Kathir ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What will become of you when you remain among the dregs of people; a folk whose pledges and trusts are corrupted, who differ and become like this? And he interlaced his fingers. He said: What do you command me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Attend to what you know, leave what you disapprove, attend to your private self, and leave their commonfolk."
"14637","14598 - Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami al-Basri informed us, who said: Munayn ibn Talib narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Abd al-Karim al-Dall narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd Allah ibn Amr ... then he mentioned the same."
"14638","14599 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to us, who said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, who said: Qurrah ibn Khalid informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him. Abd Allah ibn Amr used to say: Bring me a man who drank wine three times, and it is binding upon me to strike his neck."
"14639","14600 - Shufayy al-Asbahi: Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Haywah ibn Shurayh al-Kindi, from Shufayy, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the warrior is his reward, and for the one who equips him is his reward and the warrior's reward."
"14640","14601 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: al-Layth narrated to me, who said: Abu Qabil al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Shufayy al-Asbahi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with two books in his hand and said: Do you know what these two books are? We said: No, unless you tell us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A book from the Lord of the worlds containing the names of the people of Paradise, the names of their fathers and their tribes; then it is sealed upon the last of them, never to be increased nor decreased. And this is the book of the people of the Fire with their names, the names of their fathers and their tribes; then it is sealed upon the last of them, never to be increased nor decreased. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then what is action for, if this is a matter already finished? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather be upright and moderate; for the companion of Paradise will be sealed for him with the deed of Paradise, whatever deed he does, and the companion of the Fire will be sealed for him with the deed of the people of the Fire, whatever deed he does. Your Lord has finished with the servants. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured with his hands and cast them: Your Lord has finished with creation: a party in Paradise, and a party in the Blaze."
"14641","14602 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: al-Layth narrated to me, who said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to me, from Ibn Shufayy, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A return is like a raid; meaning: the return from a raid."
"14642","14603 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, who said: Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us. Who said: And Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qiras al-Misri narrated to us, who said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, both said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Amr, from Shufayy al-Asbahi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a thousand proverbs."
"14643","14604 - Amr ibn al-Walid ibn Abdah: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, who said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn al-Walid ibn Abdah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Then he said: Allah Almighty and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wine, gambling, the kubah, and ghubayra."
"14644","14605 - Al-Walid ibn Abdah: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: Hassan ibn Ghalib narrated to us, who said: And Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from [Yazid] ibn Abi Habib, from al-Walid ibn Abdah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... the same."
"14645","14606 - Amr ibn al-Walid: Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri Abu Habib narrated to us, who said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, who said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn al-Walid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you perceive revelation? He said: Yes; I hear ringing sounds, then I steady myself at that; and no time is revelation given to me except that I think my soul is overflowing."
"14646","14607 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn al-Walid ibn Abdah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who is with us in the house? Jibril (peace be upon him), and he has greeted you with peace."
"14647","14608 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn al-Walid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I was one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his house, and he said: Do you know who is with us in the house? I said: Who, O Messenger of Allah?! He said: Jibril (peace be upon him). I said: Peace be upon you, O Jibril, and the mercy of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has returned the greeting of peace to you."
"14648","14609 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shurayh al-Ma'afiri, he said: Sharahil ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Hudayyah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The majority of the hypocrites of my ummah are its reciters."
"14649","14610 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who the Muslim is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. They said: Then who is the believer? He said: One whom the believers trust with their lives and wealth. They said: Then who is the emigrant? He said: One who abandons evil and keeps away from it. Abu al-Qasim said: The people of Egypt say: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, while the rest of the people say: Musa ibn Ulayy; and he censured whoever called him Ulayy."
"14650","14611 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated, he said: al-Kayyis ibn Hassan narrated, from his father, from Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who the Muslim is? ... and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Salih."
"14651","14612 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Envy is only in two cases: a man to whom Allah has given the Quran, so he stands by it, declaring its lawful lawful and its unlawful unlawful; and a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he joins his kin and womb-relations with it, and acts by the word of Allah."
"14652","14613 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Salah narrated, he said: Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? I said: Yes indeed. He said: The weak and oppressed."
"14653","14614 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Amir ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man from my ummah will be called out on the Day of Resurrection before all creatures, and ninety-nine scrolls will be spread out for him, each scroll extending as far as the eye can see. Then He will say: Do you deny any of this? He will say: No, O my Lord. He will say: Do you have an excuse or a good deed? The man will be overcome with fear and say: No, O my Lord. He will say: Rather, you have good deeds with Us, and there will be no injustice against you today. Then a card will be brought out for him containing: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. His scale will weigh heavy, and he will say: O my Lord, what is this card compared with these scrolls? The scrolls will be placed in one pan, and the card in the other pan; the scrolls will fly up, and the card will weigh heavy."
"14654","14615 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Rashid ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is reconciling relations."
"14655","14616 - Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither foul-spoken nor one who affected foul speech."
"14656","14617 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated, from his father, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."
"14657","14618 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated (h). And Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Mawhab al-Ramli narrated, he said: Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyr is forgiven every sin except debt."
"14658","14619 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Being killed in the path of Allah expiates everything except debt."
"14659","14620 - Abd Allah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, he said: Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad narrated (h). And Ahmad ibn Ziyad ibn Zakariyya al-Iyadi al-A'raj narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated, from Khalid ibn Humayd al-Mahri, from Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the spoil of the gatherings of remembrance? He said: Paradise."
"14660","14621 - Abd Allah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, he said: Rishdin narrated, he said: Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: How have you woken this morning, O so-and-so? He said: I praise Allah to you, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is what I wanted from you."
"14661","14622 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated (h). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated, both said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah narrated, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrate from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is turned back from his need by augury has associated partners with Allah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, then what is its expiation? He said: He says: O Allah, there is no augury but Your augury, no good but Your good, and there is no god but You."
"14662","14623 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated, from Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, the muezzins excel us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say as the muezzin says; then when you finish, ask and you will be given."
"14663","14624 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Shurahbil, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is an enjoyment, and the best of its enjoyment is the righteous spouse."
"14664","14625 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibn Lahi'ah, both said: Shurahbil ibn Sharik al-Ma'afiri narrated, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrate from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the best of them to his companion, and the best of neighbours in the sight of Allah is the best of them to his neighbour."
"14665","14626 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor among the emigrants will precede the rich on the Day of Resurrection by forty autumns."
"14666","14627 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, he said: Shurahbil ibn Sharik reported to me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrate: that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: Some good that I do today is dearer to me than twice its like with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Hereafter concerned us while the world did not concern us, whereas today the world has inclined us toward itself."
"14667","14628 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated, he said: Haywah narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik (h). And Tahir ibn Isa ibn Qiras al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has prospered who is given sufficiency by Allah and is made content with what He has given him."
"14668","14629 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Nafi' ibn Yazid reported, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Sayf narrated to me, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: We buried a man with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when we returned and came level with his door, there was a woman coming forward whom we do not think he recognized, and he said: O Fatimah, whence have you come? She said: I have come from the family of this deceased one, showing mercy to their dead and consoling them. He said: Perhaps you reached al-kuda with them?! She said: Allah forbid that I should reach al-kuda with them, when I have heard you mention concerning them what you mention. He said: Had you reached al-kuda with them, you would not see Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it. And al-kuda means the graves."
"14669","14630 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Rabi'ah ibn Sayf, from al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14670","14631 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Rabi'ah ibn Sayf, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, the funeral procession of a disbeliever passes by us; shall we stand for it? He said: Yes, stand for it, for you do not stand for it; you only stand for the angels who are with it."
"14671","14632 - Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, from al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy; ask Allah for well-being. When you meet them, stand firm; and if they clamour and shout, then silence is incumbent upon you."
"14672","14633 - Harun narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, he said: Abu Hani' narrated to me, from al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is an enjoyment, and the best of its enjoyment is the righteous woman."
"14673","14634 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri (h). And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated (h). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy; ask Allah for well-being. When you meet them, stand firm and remember Allah much; and if they clamour and shout, then silence is incumbent upon you."
"14674","14635 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man of the Ansar: What do you say when you lie down to sleep? He said: I say: In Your name, O Allah, I lay down my side, so forgive me. He said: Allah has forgiven you."
"14675","14636 - Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: Shall I not teach you words which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach Abu Bakr when he wanted to sleep? We said: Yes indeed. He said: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You are the Lord and Sovereign of all things; I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, without partner, and the angels bear witness. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan and his association, and I seek refuge in You lest I commit evil against myself or bring it upon a Muslim."
"14676","14637 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is wounded in the head in the path of Allah and seeks reward for it, Allah will forgive him what came before of sin."
"14677","14638 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the trench, and a trench was dug around Medina, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come upon a slab of rock; we cannot dig through it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and we stood with him. When he came to it, he took the pickaxe and struck it with a blow and said takbir; I heard a crash the like of which I never heard. He said: Persia has been conquered!! Then he struck another and said takbir; I heard a crash the like of which I never heard. He said: Rome has been conquered. Then he struck another and said takbir; I heard a crash the like of which I never heard. He said: Allah has brought Himyar as helpers and supporters."
"14678","14639 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves a man for the sake of Allah, Allah has loved him, and they both enter Paradise together; the one who loved for Allah's sake will be of higher station than the other who was loved for Allah's sake."
"14679","14640 - Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, strengthens Islam by men who are not of its people."
"14680","14641 - Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated (h). And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is an enjoyment, and the best of its enjoyment is the righteous woman."
"14681","14642 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, he said: Mindal ibn Ali and Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Ma'afiri, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is an enjoyment, and the best of its enjoyment is the righteous wife."
"14682","14643 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You will overcome the non-Arabs, and you will find houses called bathhouses; no man shall enter them except with a waist-wrapper - or he said: with a lower garment - and no women shall enter them except one in childbed or out of illness."
"14683","14644 - Hafs al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated (h). And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, I ask You for health, chastity, trustworthiness, good character, and contentment with the decree."
"14684","14645 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, then the balance will be brought, then ninety-nine scrolls will be brought, each scroll extending as far as the eye can see, containing his sins and faults, and they will be placed in one pan of the balance. Then a leaf like this will be brought - and he gestured with his hand, holding his thumb - containing the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; it will be placed in the pan, and it will outweigh his sins and faults."
"14685","14646 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated (h). And Hafs al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated, both said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come upon my ummah what came upon the Children of Israel; if there was among them one who openly committed indecency with his mother, there shall be among them one who does so openly - sole matching sole. The Children of Israel split into seventy-two sects, and my ummah shall split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one sect. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: What I and my Companions are upon."
"14686","14647 - Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: Ibn An'um narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not marry women for their lineage, for their lineage may harm them; nor marry them for their wealth, for their wealth may make them insolent. A black, slit-lipped slave woman of religion is better."
"14687","14648 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja' al-Makki narrated, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after the dawn prayer except two rak'ahs."
"14688","14649 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Ghanim narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of my ummah is the likeness of rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"14689","14650 - Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Whom do you count as a martyr among you? We said: One who is killed in the path of Allah. He said: One who is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; one who drowns in the path of Allah is a martyr; one whom abdominal illness kills is a martyr; and the woman whom childbed kills is a martyr."
"14690","14651 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyr has six qualities: he is forgiven with the first gush of his blood, he is secured from the terror, he sees his seat in Paradise, he is wed to the wide-eyed houris, and he is sheltered from the punishment of the grave."
"14691","14652 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Muhammad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man belched in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Shorten your belching, for the longest in hunger on the Day of Resurrection are the most satiated in the world."
"14692","14653 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is reconciling relations."
"14693","14654 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks at a Muslim with a look that frightens him unjustly, Allah will frighten him on the Day of Resurrection."
"14694","14655 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn narrated, both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In six gatherings the believer is under Allah's guarantee so long as he is in any of them: in a congregational mosque, with a sick person, or in his funeral, or in his house, or with a just ruler whom he honours and reveres."
"14695","14656 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Knowledge is three - what is besides that is superfluous: a decisive verse, an established sunnah, and a just ordinance of inheritance."
"14696","14657 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glorification is half the balance, praise be to Allah fills the balance, and there is no god but Allah has no veil until it reaches the Most Merciful, mighty and majestic."
"14697","14658 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the swiftest supplication to be answered is the supplication of one absent for another absent."
"14698","14659 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Kathir narrated, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um al-Ifriqi, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is swifter in answer than the supplication of one absent for another absent."
"14699","14660 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated (h). And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad reported to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, does not deem too great any sin that He forgives. A man from those before you killed ninety-eight souls, then came to a monk and said: I have killed ninety-eight souls; do you find repentance for me? He said to him: You have transgressed greatly. So he rose against him and killed him. Then he came to another monk and said: I have killed ninety-nine souls; do you find repentance for me? He said: No, you have transgressed greatly. So he rose against him and killed him. Then he came to another monk and said: I have killed a hundred souls; do you find repentance for me? He said: You have transgressed greatly, and I do not know; but here are two towns, a town called Nadrah and the other called Kafrah. As for Nadrah, they do the deeds of Paradise; none but they remain in it. As for Kafrah, they do the deeds of the people of Fire; none but they remain in it. So go to Nadrah; if you remain in it and do like its people, there is no doubt of your repentance. So he set out toward it, until when he was between the two towns death overtook him. The angels asked their Lord about him, and He said: Look to which of the two towns he was nearer, and record him among its people. They found him nearer to Nadrah by a finger-joint, so he was recorded among its people."
"14700","14661 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibn Lahi'ah, Abu Hani' Humayd ibn Hani' al-Khawlani reported, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no expedition that fights in the path of Allah and gains spoils except that they hasten two-thirds of their rewards, and one-third remains; and if they gain no spoils, their reward is complete for them."
"14701","14662 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Nafi' ibn Yazid is the one, Abu Hani' narrated to me, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14702","14663 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Muqri narrated, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, he said: Abu Hani' narrated to me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman say: that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the hearts of the sons of Adam, all of them, are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful as one heart; He turns them wherever He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Turner of hearts, turn my heart to Your obedience."
"14703","14664 - Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Abu Hani', from al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, decreed the decrees before He created the heavens and the earth by fifty thousand years."
"14704","14665 - Yahya al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Nafi' ibn Yazid and al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, both said: Abu Hani' narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah finished the decrees and the affairs of the world before He created the heavens and the earth by fifty thousand years. Al-Layth did not mention 'the affairs of the world'; he only said: 'the decrees of all things'."
"14705","14666 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, he said: Khalid ibn Humayd al-Mahri narrated, he said: Humayd ibn Hani' al-Khawlani narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come upon people a time when their hearts are the hearts of non-Arabs. I said: And what are the hearts of non-Arabs? He said: Love of the world; their way is the way of the bedouins; whatever provision comes to them they put it into livestock; they regard jihad as a loss and zakat as a fine."
"14706","14667 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Abu Hani' Humayd ibn Hani' narrated to me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the poor among the emigrants will precede the rich on the Day of Resurrection by forty autumns."
"14707","14668 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah al-Hadrami reported to me, from Abu Hani' al-Khawlani, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed faith wears out in the chest of one of you as the worn-out garment wears out, [so ask Allah to] renew faith in your hearts."
"14708","14669 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Harmalah narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah reported to me, from Abu Hani', from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite this verse: {The Day mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds}. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when Allah, mighty and majestic, gathers you as arrows are gathered in the quiver, fifty thousand years, and He does not look at you."
"14709","14670 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) [came out] on the day of the trench while they were digging around Medina; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the axe and struck a blow, saying: With this blow Allah opens the treasures of Rome. Then he struck the second, saying: With this Allah opens the treasures of Persia. Then he struck the third, saying: With this blow Allah brings the people of Yemen as supporters and helpers."
"14710","14671 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: {When the earth is shaken with its mighty quaking} was sent down while Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) wept. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Bakr? He said: This surah has made me weep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did not err and did not sin, Allah would create after you a nation who sin and err, and He would forgive them."
"14711","14672 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting and the Quran shall intercede for the servant on the Day of Resurrection. Fasting will say: O Lord, I prevented him food and drink by day, so let me intercede for him. And the Quran will say: O Lord, I prevented him sleep by night, so let me intercede for him; and both will intercede."
"14712","14673 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid narrated, he said: Umar and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah (h). And Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Huyayy reported to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he bowed the two rak'ahs of dawn would lie down on his right side."
"14713","14674 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Utbah narrated (h). And Isma'il ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, both said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy ibn Abd Allah reported to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man died in Medina, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over him, then said: Would that he had died elsewhere than his birthplace. A man said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When a man dies elsewhere than his birthplace, there is measured for him from his birthplace to the end of his trace in Paradise."
"14714","14675 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy reported to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honour his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or keep silent; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honour his neighbour."
"14715","14676 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate, saying: O Allah, forgive us our sins, our wrongdoing, our jest, our earnestness, our deliberate acts; and all of that is with us."
"14716","14677 - Abu al-Zinba' narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah (h). And Isma'il ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these words: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the overwhelming of debt, the overwhelming of the enemy, and the gloating of enemies."
"14717","14678 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he wanted to sleep: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Lord of all things and God of all things, I bear witness that there is no god but You, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, and the angels bear witness. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan and his association, and I seek refuge in You lest I commit a sin against myself or bring it upon a Muslim."
"14718","14679 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the day of Badr with three hundred and twenty-five fighters, as Talut had gone out; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for them when they went out: O Allah, they are barefoot, so carry them; O Allah, they are naked, so clothe them; O Allah, they are hungry, so feed them. Allah gave them victory at Badr, and when they returned, there was not a man among them but returned with a camel or two camels, and they were clothed and satiated."
"14719","14680 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and they are from me and toward me, even if their abode be far; and it is imminent that they shall come to you as supporters and helpers, so I enjoin upon you good toward them."
"14720","14681 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My husband is poor and cannot afford anything. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her husband: Do you recite anything of the Quran? He said: I recite such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Excellent! Excellent! Your husband is rich, so keep to him. The woman kept to her husband, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, Allah has extended provision to us and given us sustenance."
"14721","14682 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: Seven men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); each man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a man, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your name? He said: Abu Ghazwan. He milked for him seven sheep, and he drank all their milk. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Would you like, O Abu Ghazwan, to accept Islam? He said: Yes. So he accepted Islam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his chest. In the morning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) milked for him one sheep, and he did not finish its milk. He said: What is the matter with you, O Abu Ghazwan? He said: By Him who sent you as a Prophet, I am satiated. He said: Yesterday you had seven intestines, and today you have but one."
"14722","14683 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to the congregational mosque, one step erases a sin and one step writes a good deed for him, going and returning."
"14723","14684 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition; they gained spoils and returned quickly. People spoke of the nearness of their raid, the abundance of their spoils, and the swiftness of their return. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not point you to one nearer in raid than them, greater in spoils, and swifter in return? One who performs ablution then goes in the morning to the mosque for the morning supererogatory prayer - he is nearer in raid, greater in spoils, and swifter in return."
"14724","14685 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The muezzins excel us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say as they say, and when you finish, ask and you will be given."
"14725","14686 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to me, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided the raid of Tabuk, he marched them by night until it was near dawn, then halted them at dawn and said: O Bilal, guard the prayer for us. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Sleep overcame Bilal, so he slept, and they slept until the sun pained them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and performed tayammum, then said to Bilal: Call the adhan and the iqamah. Bilal said: Now? He said: Yes. So they prayed after morning had come."
"14726","14687 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed in Paradise are chambers whose outside is seen from their inside and whose inside is seen from their outside. Abu Malik al-Ash'ari said: For whom are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For one who softens speech, feeds food, and stands at night while people sleep."
"14727","14688 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man to lead the people in the noon prayer; he spat toward the qiblah while leading the people in prayer. When the afternoon prayer came, he sent to another man. The first man feared, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, has something been sent down concerning me? He said: No, but you spat before you while leading the people, and you harmed Allah and His angels."
"14728","14689 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father slaughters before he prays. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell your father to pray, then slaughter."
"14729","14690 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the tormentor of the grave, and Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Will our minds be returned to us, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, as you are today. Umar said: Then it is the stone with its eye (i.e. it deserves to be struck)."
"14730","14691 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man comes visiting a sick person, let him say: O Allah, heal Your servant so-and-so; he will inflict a wound upon an enemy for You, or walk for You to a prayer."
"14731","14692 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to castrate myself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The castration of my ummah is fasting and standing in prayer."
"14732","14693 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled and halted with his Companions, when some people had made a shelter of branches over their companion while he was fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by them and said: What is the matter with your companion? Is he ill? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah, but he is fasting - and that was on a scorching day. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no righteousness in fasting while travelling."
"14733","14694 - Ali ibn Muhammad al-Ansanawi narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Huyayy narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon prayer and found a hobbled riding camel. He said: Where is the owner of this camel? No one answered him. He entered the mosque and prayed, until when he finished he came out and found the camel as it was. He said: Where is the owner of this camel? Its owner answered him, saying: I am - O Prophet of Allah - its owner. He said: Do you not fear Allah concerning it? Either feed it or release it until it seeks for itself."
"14734","14695 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated, he said: Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sun rises from its west, Iblis will fall prostrate, calling out loudly: My God, command me to prostrate to whomsoever You will. His myrmidons will gather to him and say: O their master, what is this humility? He will say: I only asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, to reprieve me until the appointed time, and this is the appointed time. He said: Then the Beast of the earth will emerge from a fissure in al-Safa. The first step it places will be at Antioch; it will come to Iblis and slap him."
"14735","14696 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr with three hundred and fifteen, like the number of the companions of Talut. When they emerged, he saw them on foot, barefoot and naked, and said: O Allah, they are hungry, so feed them; on foot, so carry them; naked, so clothe them. They returned from Badr, and there was not one of them but held the head of a camel or two camels; and they were clothed and satiated."
"14736","14697 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: My father narrated (h). And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Amr al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is silent is saved."
"14737","14698 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, Yazid ibn Amr al-Ma'afiri narrated, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is silent is saved."
"14738","14699 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Fahmi narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Amr al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - mentioning kinship, placing one of his fingers upon the other - say: Whoever joins you, I join him; whoever severs you, I sever him."
"14739","14700 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from al-Ala' ibn Kathir, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to them from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a man, saying: How do you say when you go to your bed? He said: I say: In Your name I lay down my side, so forgive me my sin. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are right; Allah has granted you success."
"14740","14701 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, [he said: My father narrated to me], from his father, from his grandfather, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from al-Ala' ibn Muhammad, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to them that Abd Allah ibn Amr heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever meets Allah on the Day of Resurrection with the five prayers, the fast of Ramadan, and bathing from major impurity, he is truly a servant of Allah; and whoever betrays any of them is truly an enemy of Allah."
"14741","14702 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Asad narrated (h). And Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated (h). And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated, they said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak reported, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, he said: Abd Allah ibn Junadah narrated to me, he said: al-Hubuli narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man milking a sheep and said: O so-and-so, when you milk, leave some for its young, for it is among the most dutiful of beasts."
"14742","14703 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, both said: Hisham ibn Ammar is the one, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of poor livelihood, and he said: Rear a small one. So I asked him? He said: A foal, a slave-girl, or a boy."
"14743","14704 - Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Marwazi narrated, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sakhr narrated to me, from Jamil ibn Kurayb, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks a mouthful of wine, flog him eighty."
"14744","14705 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, Hudayj ibn Sawmiyy narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Heedlessness is in three things: toward the remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic, from the dawn prayer until sunrise, and a man's heedlessness of himself regarding debt until it mounts him."
"14745","14706 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Knowledge is three - what is besides that is superfluous: a decisive verse, an established sunnah, and a just ordinance of inheritance."
"14746","14707 - Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, he said: Umarah ibn Ghurab al-Yahsabi narrated to me, from Abu Ghutayf al-Hadrami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were sitting; we made room for him and he sat. Then he said: Where are my companions who are from me and I am from them, and I shall enter Paradise and they shall enter it with me? He said it three times. We said: Other than us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, the people of Yemen, cast aside in the fringes of the earth, repelled from the doors of rulers; one of them dies with his need in his chest, unfulfilled."
"14747","14708 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah ibn Uqbah narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated, from Abu al-Husayn, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the time of the dawn prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed dawn in darkness, then prayed it the next day at brightness. Then he said: Where is the questioner? He said: I am. He said: The time is between yesterday and today."
"14748","14709 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad (h). And al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd Allah ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw two circles: one circle supplicating to Allah and beseeching Him, and the other learning jurisprudence and teaching it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Both circles are upon good; one of them is better than the other. As for these, they supplicate to Allah and beseech Him; if He wills He gives them, and if He wills He withholds from them. As for these, they learn and teach the ignorant; I was only sent as a teacher, and these are better. And he came to them and sat with them."
"14749","14710 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah, lawful for its females."
"14750","14711 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Rabah narrated. And Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated, both said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has forbidden to my ummah wine, gambling, mizr, kubah, and ghubayra'; and He added for me the witr prayer."
"14751","14712 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated (h). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb is the one (h). And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated (h). And Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba' narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated, all of them from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The land of the non-Arabs shall be opened for you after me, and in it are houses called bathhouses; they are forbidden for men except with waist-wrappers, and for the women of my ummah except one in childbed or ill."
"14752","14713 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi is the one, he said: Ibn al-Muhabbar narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no remembrance better than 'there is no god but Allah', nor any supplication better than seeking forgiveness. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: {So know that there is no god but Allah, and seek forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women}."
"14753","14714 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam breaks his ablution at the end of his prayer when he sits upright, his prayer is complete, and the prayer of those behind him is like his prayer."
"14754","14715 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not care what I do when I hang an amulet, or drink theriac, or utter poetry of my own accord."
"14755","14716 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, that Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to him, that Yazid ibn Rabah narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the treasures of Persia and Rome are opened for you, what manner of people will you be? Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: We shall be as Allah has commanded. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or otherwise! You will compete, then envy, then turn your backs, and hate - or the like of that - then you will go to the dwellings of the emigrants and set some of them upon the necks of others."
"14756","14717 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Qanan, from Yazid ibn Rabah Abu Firas, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Nuh (peace be upon him) fasted the lifetime except the day of Fitr and Adha; Dawud (peace be upon him) fasted half the lifetime; and Ibrahim (peace be upon him) fasted three days of every month - he fasted the lifetime and broke fast the lifetime."
"14757","14718 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Wahib ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you pray with his garment upon his nose, for that is the muzzling of Satan."
"14758","14719 - Umarah ibn Wathimah narrated to us, he said: My father Wathimah ibn Musa narrated to me, he said: Idris ibn Yahya al-Khawlani narrated, from Raja' ibn Abi Ata', from Wahib ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever feeds his brother until he satiates him, and gives him water to drink until he quenches him, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seven trenches, between every two trenches a journey of five hundred years."
"14759","14720 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: My father narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn al-Walid ibn Abdah, from Abu Asma' Sulaym ibn Bilal al-Hadrami, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There shall be a caliph, he and his offspring among the people of the Fire."
"14760","14721 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Qaysar ibn Abi Hazrah al-Tujibi (h). And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Qaysar ibn Abi Hazrah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when an old man asked him about kissing for one fasting, and he permitted him; then a young man asked him about kissing for one fasting, and he forbade him. Some people looked into the faces of others, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The old man controls himself. Musa ibn Dawud added in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew why some of you looked at others; the old man controls himself."
"14761","14722 - Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub reported, he said: Abu al-Zinba' narrated, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Hubayrah, from Abu Salim al-Jayshani, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful that a woman be married by divorcing another."
"14762","14723 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Uqbah narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah, from Abu Salim al-Jayshani, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man to marry a woman by divorcing another; nor is it lawful for a man to sell over the sale of his companion until he leaves it; nor is it lawful for three persons in a desert land that two whisper apart from their companion."
"14763","14724 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb Abu Ubayd Allah narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abu Razin al-Ghafiqi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who passes before a man while he prays deliberately shall wish on the Day of Resurrection that he were a withered tree."
"14764","14725 - Isma'il ibn Mahmud al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four, when they are in you, whatever you miss of the world does not matter: fulfilling the trust, truthfulness in speech, good character, and chastity in food."
"14765","14726 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah is the one, he said: al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Hujayrah, [from Abd Allah ibn Amr], he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the upright Muslim reaches the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer with the verses of Allah, by his good character and noble disposition."
"14766","14727 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, that Abu Suwayd narrated to him, that he heard Ibn Hujayrah report from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he says: Whoever stands in prayer with ten verses is not recorded among the heedless; whoever stands with a hundred verses is recorded among the devout; and whoever stands with a thousand verses is recorded among the grateful."
"14767","14728 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: My maternal uncle Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu al-Rabi' narrated to me, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, that Abu Suwayd narrated to him, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands in prayer with {Say: He is Allah, the One * Allah, the Eternal}, he has recited a third of the Quran."
"14768","14729 - Khayr ibn Arafah al-Tujibi narrated to us, he said: Hani' ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah al-Mahri, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Umm Ibrahim the Copt, his concubine, while she was pregnant by him with Ibrahim; he found with her a relative of hers who had come with her from Egypt; he had accepted Islam and his Islam was good, and he used to visit Umm Ibrahim. He was content, by his closeness to the concubine of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to castrate himself, cutting off what was between his legs until he left himself neither little nor much. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Umm Ibrahim one day and found her relative with her, and something occurred in his mind as occurs in the minds of people. He returned changed in colour and met Umar, informing him of what had occurred in his mind concerning the relative of Umm Ibrahim. He took his sword and hastened until he entered upon Mariyah and found that relative of hers with her; he raised the sword to kill him, but when he saw that from him, he uncovered himself. When Umar saw him, he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and informed me that Allah, mighty and majestic, has cleared her and her relative of what occurred in my mind, and gave me glad tidings that in her belly is a boy of mine, the most resembling of creatures to me; he commanded me to name him Ibrahim, and gave me the kunyah of Abu Ibrahim. Were it not that I dislike changing my kunyah by which I am known, I would take the kunyah of Abu Ibrahim, as Jibril (peace be upon him) gave me."
"14769","14730 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which Muslims are best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"14770","14731 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which Muslims are best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"14771","14732 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which Islam is best? He said: You feed food, and greet with peace those you know and those you do not know."
"14772","14733 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Aslam Abu Imran narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Amr was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a Bedouin man came forward and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love jihad and umrah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you parents? He said: Yes, both of them. He said: Then return and keep good company with them."
"14773","14734 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, Ma'ruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me (h). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Nafi' ibn Yazid is the one, Ma'ruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, that Abu Ushshanah al-Ma'afiri narrated to him that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do you know the first to enter Paradise? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The poor among the emigrants by whom hardships are warded off; one of them dies with his need in his chest, unable to fulfil it. The angels say: Our Lord, we are Your angels, Your treasurers, and the dwellers of Your heavens; do not admit them to Paradise before us. He says: My servants who associate nothing with Me, by whom hardships are warded off; one of them dies with his need in his chest, unable to fulfil it. Thereupon the angels enter upon them from every gate: {Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured; excellent is the final home}."
"14774","14735 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, from Abu Ushshanah, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first company to enter Paradise are the poor among the emigrants by whom hardships are warded off; when commanded they hear and obey, and if one of them has a need of the ruler it is not fulfilled until he dies with it in his chest. Allah, mighty and majestic, shall call Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and it shall come with its adornment and beauty. He shall say: Where are My servants who fought [in My path], were harmed in My path, and strove in My path? Enter Paradise without punishment or reckoning. The angels shall come and prostrate, saying: Our Lord, we glorify You night and day and sanctify You; who are these whom You have preferred over us? The Lord, majestic His mention, shall say: These are My servants who fought in My path, were harmed in My path, and strove in My path. Then the angels shall enter upon them from every gate: {Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured; excellent is the final home}."
"14775","14736 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Na'im, freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to him, he said: A man came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I pledge to you emigration and jihad, seeking reward from Allah. He said: Is any of your parents alive? He said: Yes, both of them. He said: Then what reward from Allah do you seek? He said: Yes. He said: Return to your parents and keep good company with them."
"14776","14737 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Sakhr, from Attab ibn Amir, he said: I was with Abd Allah ibn Amr in al-Hijr at Mecca, and he was asked about wine. He said: A man asked me, and I said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so go ask him, then return and inform me. He asked him, then returned and informed me that he asked him, and he said: It is the greatest of major sins, the mother of obscenities; whoever drinks wine abandons prayer and commits indecency with his mother, his paternal aunt, and his maternal aunt!!"
"14777","14738 - Bishr ibn Musa reported, he said: al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Attar narrated (h). And Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Sufyan, from Amr ibn Huraysh, he said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: We are in a land with neither gold nor silver; may we sell a camel for two camels, a cow for two cows, and a sheep for two sheep? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to equip an army, and the camels ran out. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the camels have run out? He said: Take from the young she-camels of charity. So I would take a camel for two camels against the charity camels."
"14778","14739 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman and Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi narrate from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall be in my ummah men whose women ride upon saddles like the semblances of riding saddles, clothed yet naked, upon their heads like the humps of Bukht camels; curse them, for they are cursed. Had there been after you a nation among the nations, they would have served them as your women serve you before you."
"14779","14740 - Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri reported, he said: My father narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Isa ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to take the day of sacrifice as a festival which He has made for this ummah. A man said: What if I find nothing but a milch animal of my family - shall I sacrifice it? He said: No; rather trim your nails, shave your pubes, and take your moustache; that is the completion of your sacrifice."
"14780","14741 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me (h). And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite. He said: Shall I teach you from those beginning with Ha-Mim? He said: O Messenger of Allah, my tongue is heavy and my liver coarse. He said: Shall I teach you from those beginning with Alif-Lam-Ra? He said to him the like of his saying. He said: Shall I teach you from the Musabbihat? He said to him the like of his first saying. He said: Upon you is the comprehensive, decisive surah; so he taught him: {When the earth is shaken with its mighty quaking}. The Bedouin said: It suffices me. Then he turned away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him back. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have been commanded with the sacrifice, so offer the rite of the day of sacrifice. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I find nothing but the sheep of my family? He said: No; rather shorten your moustache and trim your nails, for it is of the completion of your sacrifice. Al-Muqri added in his hadith: And you shave your pubes."
"14781","14742 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, that Ayyash ibn Abbas narrated to them, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me to recite .... then he mentioned the like of it."
"14782","14743 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Allah, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The servant is recorded a believer for ages upon ages, then dies while Allah is displeased with him. And the servant is recorded a disbeliever for ages upon ages, then dies while Allah is pleased with him. Whoever dies a slanderer, backbiter, and nicknamer of people, his mark on the Day of Resurrection shall be that Allah brands him upon the snout on both sides."
"14783","14744 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The souls of the believers meet at a journey's distance of a day and a night, though neither of them has seen the face of his companion."
"14784","14745 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Shuja' al-Misri narrated, from Abu al-Samh, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a piece of lead like this - pointing to the like of a pearl - were sent from heaven to earth, a journey of five hundred years, it would reach the earth before night; and if it were sent from the head of the chain, it would travel forty autumns night and day before reaching its root in its depth."
"14785","14746 - Harun ibn Mallul narrated to us, he said: al-Muqri narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Ka'b ibn Alqamah, from Isa ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned prayer and said: Whoever guards it, it shall be for him light and proof; whoever does not guard it shall have neither light nor proof, and he shall be with Pharaoh, Haman, and Ubayy ibn Khalaf."
"14786","14747 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sa'id al-Tujibi narrated to me, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies on Friday and the night of Friday is shielded from the trial of the grave."
"14787","14748 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge from seven: sudden death, the bite of the snake, being eaten by a beast, burning, drowning, that something fall upon him, and being killed fleeing from battle."
"14788","14749 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated (h). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated, from Abu Qabil, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say - when they mentioned the conquest of Constantinople and Rome, which of them would be conquered first; Abd Allah called for a chest and opened it - he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), writing what we heard from him. We said: Which of the two cities shall be conquered first, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The city of Heraclius - meaning the city of Constantinople."
"14789","14750 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the two freedmen rule - the freedman of the Arabs and the freedman of Rome - the great battles shall be at their hands."
"14790","14751 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abdus ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated, he said: Mansur ibn Ammar narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The watchword of my ummah when they are carried upon the bridge is: There is no god but You."
"14791","14752 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father Yahya ibn Khalid, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, loves whoever loves dates."
"14792","14753 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Misri narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be a tribulation in which a man parts from his brother and his father; the tribulation will fly into the hearts of men among them until the Day of Resurrection, until a man is reproached for it just as the adulteress is reproached for her adultery."
"14793","14754 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Quray'a has come to you. We said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A tribulation in which there will be the like of the egg."
"14794","14755 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Fihri narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love your beloved moderately, perhaps he will become hated to you one day; and hate the one you hate moderately, perhaps he will become your beloved one day."
"14795","14756 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated, he said: Dimam ibn Isma'il narrated, from Abu Qabil, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit at intervals, you will increase in love."
"14796","'Imran ibn 'Abd al-Ma'afiri: 14757 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um, from 'Imran ibn 'Abd al-Ma'afiri, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every debt is taken from the good deeds of its owner, except one who borrows in three cases: a man whose strength weakened in the path of Allah so he gained strength with a debt to fight his enemy, then died without repaying; a man who feared celibacy for himself so he kept chaste by marrying a woman with a debt, then died without repaying; and a man with whom a Muslim man died and he found nothing to suffice him except with a debt, then died without repaying - it will be repaid on their behalf on the Day of Resurrection."
"14797","14758 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, 'Imran ibn 'Abd narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three: whoever borrows in these then dies without repaying, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, repays on his behalf: a man who is in the path of Allah and his strength weakens, so he gains strength with a debt against his enemy, then dies without repaying; a man with whom a man among you dies and he finds nothing to suffice him nor to cover him except with a debt, then dies without repaying; and a man who fears temptation for himself in celibacy so he keeps chaste by marrying a woman with a debt, then dies without repaying - for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, repays on their behalf on the Day of Resurrection."
"14798","14759 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, 'Imran ibn 'Abd al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose prayer is not accepted: one who leads a people while they dislike him; a man who comes to prayer dibaran - and dibar is coming after the time; and a man who enslaves his freedman."
"14799","The hadiths of Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, his kunya Abu Jafar, his mother Asma bint 'Umays ibn al-Nu'man ibn Ka'b ibn Malik ibn Quhafah ibn Khath'am, and Abd Allah was born in the land of Abyssinia. Mention of the age of Abd Allah ibn Jafar and his death: 14760 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, he said: And in it died Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib in Madinah, his kunya Abu Jafar - meaning the year eighty."
"14800","14761 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated, he said: Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar used to dye with henna."
"14801","What has reached us of the Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14762 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of al-Maghazi, narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of qasab, in which there is no noise and no fatigue."
"14802","14763 - al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that they both came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they were seven years old, and when he saw them he smiled, extended his hand, and pledged allegiance to them."
"14803","14764 - Abu Salih al-Qasim ibn al-Layth al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, he said: My father narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: When Abu Talib died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to al-Ta'if walking on his feet, and he called them to Islam but they did not answer him. So he turned away, came to the shade of a tree, prayed two rak'ahs, then said: O Allah, to You I complain of the weakness of my strength, the scantiness of my means, and my lowliness before people; O Most Merciful of the merciful, You are the Most Merciful of the merciful - to whom do You entrust me? To an enemy who frowns at me, or to a near one to whom You have given charge of my affair? If You are not angry with me, I do not care; Your well-being is broader for me. I seek refuge in the light of Your Face by which darknesses shone and by which the affair of this world and the Hereafter was set right, from Your anger descending upon me or Your displeasure alighting upon me. To You is the right of reproach until You are pleased, and there is no power except through You."
"14804","14765 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Malik narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating watermelon with fresh dates."
"14805","What Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn transmitted from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14766 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated, he said: Shayban narrated, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped after he was poisoned."
"14806","14767 - Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Aslami narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted and Mighty, is with the debtor until he repays his debt, so long as his debt is not in what Allah dislikes."
"14807","14768 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, he said: Ali ibn Abi Ali al-Hashimi narrated, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him behind him, and said: O boy, shall I not give you? Shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you? Guard Allah, He will guard you; guard Allah, you will find Him before you; when you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah; and know that the Pen has dried upon what is to be; and know that if creation wished you something not written upon you, they could not reach you with it; and know that victory is with patience, relief is with distress, and with hardship is ease."
"14808","What Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar transmitted from his father: 14769 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah ibn Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, he said: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two garments dyed with saffron, a cloak and a turban."
"14809","What Mu'awiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar transmitted from his father: 14770 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting a ram with arrows, and said: Do not mutilate animals."
"14810","14771 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over Hamzah on the day of Uhud while he was burying him; he was wrapped in a striped cloak, and his feet showed when they covered his head, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered harmal, and it was placed upon his feet, and he said: Were it not that our women would grieve at that, we would have left him in the open for the well-being of the beasts and birds."
"14811","14772 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Abu Hamid al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Abu Zur'ah 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Karim narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Jafar ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib narrated, my uncle Musa ibn Jafar narrated, from Salih ibn Mu'awiyah, from his brother Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiyah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ali is my root, and Jafar is my branch - or: Jafar is my root, and Ali is my branch."
"14812","Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father: 14773 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Harun ibn Musa al-Awdi narrated, he said: Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashja'i narrated, from Makhramah ibn Bukayr, from his father, from Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings to you, O Abd Allah - your father flies with the angels in the heaven."
"14813","Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father: 14774 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father, concerning these words: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Magnificent; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Teach them to your dying ones. They said: O Messenger of Allah, then how are they for the living? He said: Better and better."
"14814","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from his father: 14775 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Mawhab narrated, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed him, from his father, he said: I was with Abd Allah ibn Jafar when a man came and said: Command me supplications by which Allah will benefit me. He said: Yes - I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a man asked him about what you asked me, and he said: Ask Allah pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter."
"14815","al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14776 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated. And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated me behind him one day, and confided to me a hadith I do not narrate to any of the people. He said: And the most beloved thing with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) screened himself was a target or a dense stand of palms. He entered the garden of a man of the Ansar, and there was a camel; when it saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it yearned and its eyes shed tears. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and wiped its hump and its temples, and it calmed. Then he said: Whose is this camel? A youth of the Ansar came and said: It is mine, O Messenger of Allah. He said to him: Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast which Allah has made you own? For it has complained to me that you starve it and overwork it."
"14816","14777 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il al-Minqari narrated, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and appointed over them Zayd ibn Harithah: if he is killed or martyred, your commander is Ja'far ibn Abi Talib; if he is killed or martyred, your commander is Abd Allah ibn Rawahah. They went and met the enemy. Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed; then Ja'far took the banner and fought until he was killed; then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed, or martyred; then a sword of the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner, and Allah gave victory through him. News of them reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he went out, ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed - your brothers met the enemy; Zayd ibn Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed - or martyred - then Ja'far took the banner and fought until he was killed - or martyred - then Abd Allah ibn Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed - or martyred - then a sword of the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner, and Allah gave victory through him. Then he gave the family of Ja'far three days respite from coming to them, then came to them and said: Do not weep for him after today. Then he said: Call for me the sons of my brother; we were brought as though chicks. He said: Call for me the barber; he ordered him and he shaved our heads. Then he said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib; as for 'Awn, he resembles my creation and character. Then he took my hand and lifted it, and said: O Allah, succeed Ja'far in his family, and bless Abd Allah in the transaction of his right hand - he said it three times. He said: Our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you fear poverty for them, while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?!"
"14817","Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14778 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating cucumber with fresh dates."
"14818","al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14779 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a prophet to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"14819","14780 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated, he said: Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: He forbade killing them - meaning the snakes that are in houses."
"14820","al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14781 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated, he said: Abd al-Muhaymin ibn 'Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi narrated, from his father, that Sahl entered upon al-Hajjaj while he was leaning on his hand, and said to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Ansar: Do good to their doers of good, and pardon their offenders. He said: Who testifies for you? He said: These your two flanks: Abd Allah ibn Jafar and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah. They said: Yes."
"14821","Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14782 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdous al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said to Ibn 'Abbas and Abd Allah ibn Jafar: Do you remember the day we met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes; he carried us and left you."
"14822","Muwarriq al-'Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14783 - Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, he said: Shu'bah narrated, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Muwarriq al-'Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried a boy of Banu Hashim and the son of Jafar upon a camel."
"14823","14784 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated, Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Muwarriq al-'Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came from a journey, would be met by the children of his household; he came from a journey, and I was raced forward to him, so he carried me before him, then one of the two sons of Fatimah was brought and he carried him behind him, and we entered Madinah three upon a mount."
"14824","14785 - Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated, he said: 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated, from Muwarriq, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14825","14786 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Muwarriq al-'Ijli, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried a boy of Banu Hashim and the son of Jafar upon a mount."
"14826","Khalid ibn Sarah al-Makhzumi, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14787 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated - both from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ja'far ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: When the news of Jafar's death came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Jafar, for there has come to them a matter that occupies them."
"14827","14788 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ja'far ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was with lads of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and he carried me and another boy upon the mount he was upon, so we were three upon it."
"14828","14789 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ja'far ibn Khalid, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head three times, and said: O Allah, succeed Jafar in his family."
"14829","'Ubayd ibn Umm Kilab, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14790 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated. And Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from 'Ubayd, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Jafar say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sneezed he praised Allah, and it would be said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, and he would say: May Allah guide you and set right your state."
"14830","'Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14791 - Idris ibn Jafar al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated. And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated - both from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd Allah ibn Musafi' informed me, from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from 'Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever doubts in anything of his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations so long as he has not given salam."
"14831","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14792 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a silver ring on his right hand."
"14832","14793 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', that Abd Allah ibn Jafar said to his daughter when he brought her in to al-Hajjaj: When he comes to you, say: There is no god but Allah, the Exalted, the Magnificent; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say it when hardship befell him. So she said it, and he did not reach her."
"14833","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14794 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated. And 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated - both said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a ring on his right hand."
"14834","14795 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Nu'man al-Shaybani narrated, he said: Yahya ibn al-'Ala narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a ring on his right hand."
"14835","14796 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I saw the ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his right hand."
"14836","Budayh, freedman of Abd Allah ibn Jafar, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14797 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated, he said: Abu 'Asim narrated, from Juwayriyah ibn Asma, from 'Isa ibn 'Umar, from Budayh, he said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar came as a delegation to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan; he entered upon him while Yahya ibn al-Hakam was with him, and he asked him: How did you leave Khabithah - meaning Madinah? Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it Taybah, and you call it Khabithah?!"
"14837","A shaykh of Fahm called Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14798 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated, he said: Mis'ar narrated, from a shaykh of Fahm, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"14838","14799 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Mis'ar, from a man of Fahm called Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"14839","Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar: 14800 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Raja al-'Abbadani narrated, he said: Salamah ibn Raja narrated, from Yazid ibn 'Iyad, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots at night is not of us; and whoever sleeps upon a roof with no wall then falls and dies, his blood is void."
"14840","Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam, his kunya Abu Khubayb, also kunya Abu Bakr; his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, her mother Qutaylah bint Abd al-'Uzza ibn Abd Allah ibn Nasr ibn Malik ibn Hisl ibn 'Amir ibn Lu'ayy. Mention of the age of Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, his death, and some of his reports: 14801 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn 'Ubayd narrated, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr was killed in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year seventy-three, and on the day he was killed he was seventy-two years old."
"14841","14802 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr was born in Madinah twenty months after the Hijrah, and he is older than al-Miswar and Marwan by four months and seven days."
"14842","14803 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated, from al-Haytham ibn 'Adi, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr was killed in the year seventy-two."
"14843","14804 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Urwah narrated to me, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to me, from his father, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr went out when she emigrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was pregnant with Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr; she gave birth to him, brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to tahnik him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him and placed him in his lap; a date was brought, he sucked it then placed it in his mouth, and did tahnik for him with it - so the first thing to enter his belly was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Asma said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped him and named him Abd Allah. Then he came afterwards, seven or eight years old, to pledge allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - al-Zubayr ordered him to do so - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw him coming, and pledged him. He was the first born in Islam in Madinah after the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Jews would say: We have bewitched them so no child is born to them in Madinah. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir when Abd Allah was born. And Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said - when he heard the takbir of the people of Sham, who had killed Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: Those who said takbir at his birth are better than those who said takbir at his killing."
"14844","14805 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, and Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, she said: Asma bint Abi Bakr went out when she emigrated while she was pregnant with Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr; she arrived at Quba and gave birth to Abd Allah at Quba. Then she went out with him after she gave birth to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to tahnik him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him from her and placed him in his lap, then called for a date. 'A'ishah said: We remained a while seeking it before we found it; he sucked it, then placed it in his mouth - so the first thing to enter his belly was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Asma said: Then he wiped him, supplicated for him, and named him Abd Allah. Then he came afterwards, seven or eight years old, to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - al-Zubayr ordered him to do so - and he smiled when he saw him coming to him, then pledged him."
"14845","14806 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Awn al-Wasiti narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, all my companions have kunyas, so give me a kunya. He said: Take a kunya by your son Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr. And she used the kunya Umm Abd Allah until she died."
"14846","14807 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Awn al-Wasiti narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, that 'A'ishah said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): All your women have kunyas except me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Take the kunya Umm Abd Allah. She was called Umm Abd Allah until she died, though she never gave birth at all."
"14847","14808 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated, he said: My father Maslamah ibn Qa'nab narrated to me, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from 'Abbad ibn Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not give me a kunya? He said: Take a kunya by Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr. So she was called Umm Abd Allah."
"14848","14809 - Ali ibn al-Saqr al-Sukuni narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from 'Abbad ibn Hamzah, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14849","14810 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated, that when death came to Mu'awiyah, he said to Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah: I have smoothed the lands for you and spread the people for you; I fear none for you but the people of the Hijaz. If any doubt comes to you from them, direct to them Muslim ibn 'Uqbah al-Murri, for I have tried him more than once and found none like him, for his obedience and counsel. When the opposition of Ibn al-Zubayr and his call to himself reached Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah, he called Muslim ibn 'Uqbah al-Murri, who had been struck by paralysis, and said: The Commander of the Believers enjoined upon me in his illness that if any doubt from the people of the Hijaz comes to me, I direct you to them - and doubt has come to me. He said: I am as the Commander of the Believers thought; conclude for me and array the armies. He said: He came to Madinah and permitted it three days, then called them to the pledge of Yazid upon that they are owned slaves in obedience to Allah and disobedience to Him; they answered him to that, except one man of Quraysh whose mother was an umm walad. He said to him: Pledge to Yazid upon that you are a slave in obedience to Allah and disobedience to Him. He said: No - rather in obedience to Allah. He refused to accept that from him, and killed him. His mother swore an oath: if Allah enables her over Muslim, alive or dead, she will burn him with fire! He said: When Muslim ibn 'Uqbah left Madinah his illness intensified and he died. The mother of the Qurashi went out with slaves of hers to the grave of Muslim, ordered it dug from the head side; when they reached him, there was a serpent coiled upon his neck, gripping the tip of his nose, sucking it. He said: The people shrank from it and said: O our mistress, turn back - Allah has sufficed you his evil; they told her the news. She said: No, until I fulfil to Allah what I promised Him. Then she said: Dig for me from the feet side; they dug, and there was the serpent winding its tail about his feet. He said: She withdrew, prayed two rak'ahs, then said: O Allah, if You know I was only angry at Muslim ibn 'Uqbah today for You, then leave him between me and him. He said: Then she took a stick, went to the serpent's tail, moved it, and it slipped from the back of his head and left the grave. Then she ordered him taken out of the grave and burned with fire."
"14850","14811 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: A companion of ours informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq informed me, he said: I heard Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq say: I was present at the killing of Ibn al-Zubayr on the day he was killed in the Sacred Mosque. The armies began entering through the mosque gates; whenever people entered through a gate, he charged them alone until he drove them out. While he was in that state, a battlement of the mosque's battlements came and fell upon his head, and felled him, while he was reciting these verses, saying:"
"14851","14812 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: Nothing Ka'b used to tell us but has come as he said, except his saying: a youth of Thaqif will kill me - and here is his head before me - meaning al-Mukhtar. Ibn Sirin said: Not knowing that Abu Muhammad was hidden for him - meaning al-Hajjaj."
"14852","14813 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated, he said: al-Qasim ibn Ma'n narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, he said: When Mu'awiyah died, Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr held back from obedience to Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah and openly reviled him; that reached Yazid, so he swore he would only be brought to him fettered, or he would send to him. It was said to Ibn al-Zubayr: Shall we not make for you fetters of silver over which you wear a garment, and fulfil his oath - for reconciliation befits you? He said: I will not - by Allah - fulfil his oath. Then he said: Then he said: By Allah, a strike with a sword in honour is dearer to me than a strike with a whip in humiliation. Then he called to himself and openly opposed Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah; Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah directed to him Muslim ibn 'Uqbah al-Murri with the army of the people of Sham, and ordered him to fight the people of Madinah, and when finished with that to march to Makkah. He said: Muslim ibn 'Uqbah entered Madinah, the remnants of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fled from him, he wrought havoc in it and was excessive in killing, then left it; when he was on part of the road to Makkah he died, and appointed Husayn ibn Numayr al-Kindi as successor, saying to him: O son of the donkey's pack-saddle, beware the deceptions of Quraysh, and deal with them only with the fetter, then with the harvest. Husayn marched until he reached Makkah and fought Ibn al-Zubayr there days; Ibn al-Zubayr pitched a tent in the mosque, in which were women giving drink to the wounded, treating them, feeding the hungry, and concealing the wounded with them. Husayn said: There keeps coming out to us from that tent a lion as it comes out of its den - who will suffice me it? A man of the people of Sham said: I. When night darkened upon him, he placed a candle at the tip of his spear, then spurred his horse, then pierced the tent and it blazed fire; the Ka'bah that day was draped with coverings, upon its top the hibarah; the wind flew with the flame upon the Ka'bah until it burned, and burned in it that day the two horns of the ram with which Ishaq was ransomed. He said: News of the death of Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah reached Husayn ibn Numayr, so Husayn ibn Numayr fled. When Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah died, Marwan ibn al-Hakam called to himself; the people of Hims, Jordan and Palestine answered him. Ibn al-Zubayr directed to him al-Dahhak ibn Qays al-Fihri with a hundred thousand; they met at Marj Rahit, Marwan that day with five thousand of Banu Umayyah, their freedmen and followers of the people of Sham. Marwan said to a freedman of his called Karrah: Charge whichever flank you wish. He said: How shall I charge them, for their numbers? He said: They are between coerced and hired - charge them, may you have no mother; piercing combat will suffice you the army; they will suffice you themselves - they are but slaves of dinar and dirham. He charged them and routed them; al-Dahhak ibn Qays was killed and the army broke. Concerning that Zufar ibn al-Harith says verses. He said: Then Marwan died; Abd al-Malik called to himself and rose; the people of Sham answered him. He addressed upon the pulpit: Who is for Ibn al-Zubayr among you? Al-Hajjaj said: I, O Commander of the Believers. He silenced him, then he returned and he silenced him. He said: I, O Commander of the Believers, for I saw in a dream that I stripped off his cloak and wore it. He concluded for him with the army to Makkah until he came to Ibn al-Zubayr there and fought him. Ibn al-Zubayr said to the people of Makkah: Guard these two mountains, for you will remain in good, mighty, so long as they do not appear upon them. He said: They did not remain but al-Hajjaj and those with him appeared upon Abu Qubays and set upon it the catapult, with which he pelted Ibn al-Zubayr and those with him in the mosque. On the morning in which Ibn al-Zubayr was killed, Ibn al-Zubayr entered upon his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr, she that day a hundred years old, no tooth fallen, no sight spoiled. She said to her son: O Abd Allah, what have you done in your war? He said: They have reached such-and-such place. He said: Ibn al-Zubayr laughed and said: In death there is rest. She said: O my son, perhaps you wish it for me - I do not love to die until I come upon one of your two ends: either you rule, and my eye is gladdened by that, or you are killed and I reckon you. He said: He bade her farewell; she said to him: O my son, beware giving a trait of your religion out of fear of killing. He left her and entered the mosque, having placed two door-leaves upon the Black Stone fearing the catapult would strike it. A comer came to Ibn al-Zubayr while he was sitting at the Stone and said to him: Shall we not open the Ka'bah for you to ascend into it? Abd Allah looked at him, then said to him: From everything you guard your brother except from himself - meaning his death - and does the Ka'bah have a sanctity this place does not? By Allah, if they found you clinging to the Ka'bah's curtains they would kill you! It was said to him: Will you not speak to them of reconciliation? He said: Is this a time of reconciliation? By Allah, if they found you inside it they would slaughter you all. Then he began reciting verses. Then he turned to the family of al-Zubayr admonishing them, saying: Let each of you sheath his sword as he sheaths his face; let him not lower his sword and defend himself with his hand as though a woman. By Allah, I never met a host but in the first squadron, and I never felt a wound but the pain of the remedy. He said: While they were thus, a group entered upon them through the gate of Banu Jumah, among them a black man. He said: Who are these? It was said: The people of Hims. He charged them with two swords; the first he met was the black man, he struck him with his sword until he severed his leg. The black man said: Ow! O son of the adulteress. Ibn al-Zubayr said to him: Silence, O son of Ham - is Asma an adulteress? Then he drove them from the mosque and returned; there were people who had entered through the gate of Banu Sahm. He said: Who are these? It was said: The people of Jordan. He charged them, saying verses; he drove them from the mosque. There were people who had entered through the gate of Banu Makhzum; he charged them, saying verses. He said: Upon the mosque's roof were supporters of his pelting his enemy with bricks and other. He charged them, and a brick struck him in the part of his head until it split his head; he stood upright saying verses. He said: Then he fell; two freedmen of his bent over him, saying verses. He said: Then he was gone to and his head was cut off."
"14853","14814 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, he said: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated, he said: Abu Nawfal ibn Abi 'Aqrab al-'Urayji narrated to me, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf crucified Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr upon the pass of Madinah to show that to Quraysh. When they dispersed they would pass and not stand over him, until Abd Allah ibn 'Umar passed, stood over him, and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubayb - he said it three times - then said: I forbade you this - he said it three times - you were fasting much, praying at night much, joining kinship. That reached al-Hajjaj - the standing of Abd Allah ibn 'Umar - so he had him taken down and cast him in the graves of the Jews, and sent to Asma bint Abi Bakr to come to him, her sight having gone; she refused, so he sent to her: You shall surely come or I shall surely send to you one who drags you by your forelocks. She said: By Allah, I shall not come to you until you send to me one who drags me by my forelocks. His messenger came and told him; he said: O boy, hand me my sandals; he handed him his shoes; he rose burning until he came to her, and said to her: How did you see Allah do with the enemy of Allah? She said: I saw you spoiled his world, and he spoiled your Hereafter; as for what you used to reproach him with Dhat al-Nitaqayn - indeed, I had two waist-wraps: a wrap with which the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was covered from ants, and my other wrap which women must have; and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Thaqif is a destroyer and a liar. As for the liar, we have seen him; as for the destroyer, you are he. He said: He went out."
"14854","14815 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, he said: Abu al-Muhayyah narrated, from his father, he said: I came to Makkah after Ibn al-Zubayr was crucified - or killed - by three days. His mother Asma bint Abi Bakr spoke to al-Hajjaj: Has it not come time for this rider to come down? He said: The hypocrite? She said: No, by Allah, he was no hypocrite; he was fasting much, praying at night much. He said: Be silent, for you are an old woman who has doted. She said: I have not doted since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall come out of Thaqif a liar and a destroyer. As for the liar we have seen him - meaning al-Mukhtar - as for the destroyer, you are he."
"14855","14816 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn 'Amr al-Dabbi narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Qays ibn al-Ahnaf al-Thaqafi, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Asma bint Abi Bakr came with slave-girls of hers, her sight having gone, and said: Where is al-Hajjaj? We said: He is not here. She said: Order him to order for us these bones, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid mutilation. We said: When he comes we shall tell him. She said: When he comes, tell him I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Thaqif is a liar and a destroyer."
"14856","14817 - 'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abu Zayd ibn Abi al-Ghimr narrated, he said: Dimam ibn Isma'il narrated, from 'Uqayl ibn Khalid, that his father was with al-Hajjaj when Ibn al-Zubayr was killed; he sent him to Asma bint Abi Bakr, saying to him: Tell her: al-Hajjaj says to you: Separate what was yours of wealth from the wealth of Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr. She said: Has he done it with the son of Asma? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There shall come out of this clan of Thaqif two men: one lies, the other is a destroyer. As for the liar we have known him; I think him none but the destroyer. I returned to him and told him, and he did not dislike that."
"14857","'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: 14818 - 'Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Announce marriage."
"14858","14819 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: The name of Abu Bakr was Abd Allah ibn 'Uthman; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him 'Atiq, freed from the Fire."
"14859","14820 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated, he said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated, he said: Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated, from his uncle 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: It was revealed concerning Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: And no one has with him any favour to be repaid, but seeking the Face of his Lord, the Most High; and he shall surely be pleased."
"14860","14821 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd informed me, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to point with his finger when he supplicated, not moving it. Ibn Jurayj said: 'Amr ibn Dinar added, he said: 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating thus, leaning with his left hand upon his left leg."
"14861","14822 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, he said: 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in prayer, he placed his left leg between his thigh and his shin, placed his left hand upon his left thigh, and placed his right hand upon his right thigh."
"14862","14823 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed and sat in the two or the four, place his left hand upon his left thigh, place his right hand upon his right thigh, and point with the finger next to the thumb."
"14863","14824 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he prayed he placed one hand upon his left thigh and the other hand upon his right thigh, his finger thus pointing."
"14864","14825 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, when he began prayer raise his hands until he passed them beyond his ears."
"14865","14826 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to me, he said: My father Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated, from 'Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I came to my father, and he said: Where were you? I said: I found people than whom I have seen none better; they remember Allah and one of them trembles until he swoons from fear of Allah, so I sat with them. He said: Do not sit with them after this. He saw me as though that had not taken hold in me, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite the Quran, and I saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar recite the Quran, and this does not befall them - do you deem them less fearful of Allah than Abu Bakr and 'Umar? I saw that it was so, and left them."
"14866","'Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father: 14827 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated, from 'Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday, let him bathe."
"14867","14828 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated, he said: My father narrated. And Muhammad ibn Zuhayr Abu Ya'la al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: 'Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated, he said: 'Ubayd ibn 'Aqil narrated, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, he said: Ibn Ishaq narrated, he said: Yahya ibn 'Abbad narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Quraysh had wailed over their slain, then regretted, and said: Do not wail over them lest that reach Muhammad and his companions and they gloat over you. Among the captives was Abu Wada'ah ibn Subayrah al-Sahmi; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has in Makkah a merchant son, clever, wealthy - as though you see him having come to you for his father's ransom. When Quraysh said concerning ransom what they said, al-Muttalib said: You have spoken the truth; by Allah, if you do, he will gain advantage over you. Then he slipped away by night, arrived at Madinah, and ransomed his father for four thousand dirhams."
"14868","Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandfather: 14829 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisli al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that there was between him and 'Amr ibn al-Zubayr a dispute; Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr entered upon Sa'id ibn al-'As while 'Amr was with him upon the couch. Sa'id said to Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: Here. He said: No - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that the two disputants sit before the judge."
"14869","14830 - Muhammad ibn Abi Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated. And al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, he said: Sa'dan ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated, from Mus'ab ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he broke fast with a people, said: The fasting have broken fast with you, and the angels have invoked blessings upon you."
"14870","14831 - al-'Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn 'Amr ibn Sikkin al-Duba'i narrated, he said: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, he said: Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated, he said: Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a group of his companions while something had come before them that made them laugh, and said: Do you laugh while the mention of Paradise and Hell is before you? Then this verse was revealed: Inform My servants that I am the Forgiving, the Merciful; and that My punishment is the painful punishment."
"14871","Nafi' ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandfather: 14832 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Nafi' ibn Thabit narrated, from his brother, from his father Nafi' ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two or three times."
"14872","14833 - al-'Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sa'iqah narrated, he said: Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated, he said: Ibn Abi al-Mawwal narrated, he said: Nafi' ibn Thabit informed me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed 'Isha he bowed four rak'ahs, made witr with a prostration, then slept until he prayed afterwards his prayer of the night."
"14873","Yahya ibn 'Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandfather: 14834 - Muhammad ibn Khalaf the judge Waki' narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Shabib al-Madani narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from Yahya ibn 'Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his grandfather Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for al-Zubayr in the year of Khaybar four shares: a share for al-Zubayr, a share for the near kin, a share for his mother, and a share for his horse."
"14874","'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14835 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to me, from 'Urwah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One suckling does not make unlawful, nor two sucklings."
"14875","14836 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling does not make unlawful, nor two sucklings."
"14876","14837 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14877","14838 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Urwah narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I wished that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given us the call to prayer. I said: Why is that? He said: Because they are the longest-necked of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection."
"14878","14839 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah al-Tinnisi narrated, he said: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Umra is valid for whom it is given, and ruqba for whom it is given - its way is the way of inheritance."
"14879","14840 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Abi 'Abbad al-Makki narrated, he said: Abu Usamah narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, concerning the word of Allah: Take pardon, he said: Allah commanded His Prophet to take pardon from the characters of people."
"14880","14841 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated, he said: 'Umar ibn Ali narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: This verse was revealed concerning the Negus: And when they hear what was sent down to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears."
"14881","14842 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated, he said: Hunayfah ibn Marzuq narrated, he said: Sharik narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Who eats the crow, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it fasiq?!"
"14882","14843 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated. And al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated. And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn Hubab al-Jumahi narrated, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated - they said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him: that a man of the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the streams of al-Harrah with which they watered the palms. The Ansari said: Release the water. Al-Zubayr refused him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water, O Zubayr, then send to your neighbour. The Ansari grew angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is your aunt's son? The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed colour, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water, O Zubayr, then hold the water until it returns to the wall. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, I deem this verse was revealed concerning that: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what disputes between them - the verse."
"14883","14844 - Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple of my ummah."
"14884","Abd Allah ibn 'Urwah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14845 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn 'Urwah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The House was only named al-'Atiq because Allah freed it from tyrants."
"14885","Yusuf, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14846 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, shall I perform Hajj on behalf of my father? He said: Are you his eldest child? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on his behalf."
"14886","14847 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn al-Zubayr, that Zam'ah had a slave-girl he used to tread, and they suspected her; she gave birth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sawdah: As for inheritance, it is his; as for you, veil yourself from him, O Sawdah, for he is no brother to you."
"14887","14848 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated, he said: Qays and Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he assigned him inheritance, because he was born upon the bed of Zam'ah, and said to Sawdah: As for you, veil yourself from him."
"14888","14849 - 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated, from Za'idah, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn al-Zubayr - or from a freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr - from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Zam'ah used to tread a slave-girl... then he mentioned the like of it."
"14889","al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14850 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisli narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: Of the sunnah of the pilgrim is to pray on the day of Tarwiyah Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, the latter 'Isha and Fajr at Mina, then go in the morning and rest midday where Allah has written for him, then go in the afternoon when the sun declines, address the people, then descend and join the two prayers, Zuhr and 'Asr, then stand at 'Arafah, depart when the sun sets, then pray Maghrib where Allah has decreed for him to pray, then stand at Muzdalifah; when dawn rises pray Fajr, then depart in the morning; when he stones the Jamrah, what was forbidden to him is lawful except women, until he circumambulates the House."
"14890","'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14851 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Arim narrated, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from 'Ata, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque; and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a prayer in my mosque by a thousand prayers."
"14891","14852 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hujr al-Basri narrated, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated, from Khallad ibn 'Ata, he said: I heard 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah say: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Sacred Mosque is favoured over my mosque by a hundred prayers."
"14892","14853 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated, he said: 'Ata narrated, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr addressed us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"14893","14854 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An 'umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"14894","14855 - Muhammad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated, he said: Abu al-Jawwab narrated, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated, from Layth, from 'Ata, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: They did not used to wash their posteriors with water."
"14895","Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14856 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrate that Ibn al-Zubayr wrote to the people of Iraq: The one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - If I were taking a close friend until I meet Allah other than Allah, I would have taken Abu Bakr as close friend - used to make the grandfather a father."
"14896","14857 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bahr al-Hujaymi narrated, he said: Sa'id ibn Salim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever recites the Quran openly or by looking, he is given a tree in Paradise - if a crow hatched under a leaf of it, then that chick grew and rose, old age would reach it before it crossed that leaf."
"14897","14858 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated, he said: Nafi' ibn 'Umar narrated, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: that al-Aqra' ibn Habis came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint him over his people. 'Umar said: Do not appoint him, O Messenger of Allah. They spoke before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until their voices rose. Abu Bakr said to 'Umar: You intended only to oppose me. He said: I did not intend to oppose you. He said: Then was revealed: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet. After that, when 'Umar spoke before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his speech was not heard until he was asked to make it understood."
"14898","14859 - Ja'far ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: My father narrated. And Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated, they said: Hajjaj narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me: that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr informed them: that a party of Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them al-Aqra' ibn Habis. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint al-Aqra' over his people. 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, do not appoint him. They disputed until their voices rose. Abu Bakr said: You intended only to oppose me. 'Umar said: I did not intend to oppose you. They argued until their voices rose; there was revealed concerning that: O you who believe, do not put forward before Allah and His Messenger - until the end of the verse."
"14899","14860 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, that Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl; that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Fatimah is but a part of me; what harms her harms me, and what wearies her wearies me."
"14900","'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14861 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no owner of camels but he is brought on the Day of Resurrection, if he did not render its due, and it walks upon him in a plain, treading him with its feet. The owner of cattle is brought, if he did not render its due, and it walks upon him in a plain, treading him with its hooves and goring him with its horns. The owner of sheep is brought, if he did not render its due, and it walks upon him in a plain, goring him with its horns and treading him with its hooves - none among them hornless nor broken-horned. And the owner of treasure is brought, and a bald serpent is fashioned for him, and he finds nothing, so he puts his hand in its mouth. 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated it from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr al-Laythi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mursal."
"14901","14862 - 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated, he said: Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Zubayr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is taken to account with scrutiny is destroyed."
"14902","14863 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Asfahani narrated to us, he said: 'Aqil ibn Yahya al-Tihrani narrated, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: It is not of the sunnah to invoke blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday upon the pulpit."
"14903","14864 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Buzuri narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Musa al-Ta'ifi narrated, from Muslim ibn Ruzayq al-Makhzumi, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his uncle al-'Abbas to order his sons to plough al-qadb, for it removes poverty. He said: And al-qadb is al-rutbah."
"14904","Tawus ibn Kaysan, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14865 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi narrated, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever unsheathes his sword then lays it - his blood is void. Meaning 'lays it': strikes with it."
"14905","al-'Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14866 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati and Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, they said: Abu Nu'aym narrated, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated, from al-'Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr upon the pulpit of Makkah say in his sermon: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If the son of Adam were given a valley of gold, he would love a second to it; if given a second, he would love a third to it; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever turns."
"14906","Abu al-Hakam 'Imran al-Sulami, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14867 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from 'Imran al-Sulami, he said: I came to Ibn al-Zubayr and asked him about nabidh, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar and the gourd."
"14907","14868 - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub the judge narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, he said: Shu'bah narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami, he said: I asked Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jar and the gourd."
"14908","al-Hasan ibn Yannaq, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14869 - Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated, he said: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated, from Ibrahim ibn Nafi', from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were taking a close friend other than my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as close friend; but he is my brother and my companion in the cave."
"14909","'Abidah ibn 'Amr al-Salmani, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14870 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated, he said: Shu'bah narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from 'Ubaydah, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man swore by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, falsely - and he was forgiven."
"14910","Abd Allah al-Bahi, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14871 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, he said: Abu Nu'aym Dirar ibn Surad narrated. And Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated - they said: Ali ibn 'Abis narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Bahi, freedman of al-Zubayr, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating until al-Hasan ibn Ali came and climbed upon his back; he did not put him down until he was the one who came down, and he would spread his legs for him so he entered from this side and exited from the other side."
"14911","14872 - al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated, he said: Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated, from 'Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Bahi, from Ibn al-Zubayr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed so-and-so and his child upon this pulpit."
"14912","Abd Allah ibn 'Amir ibn Kurayz, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14873 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Mus'ab ibn Thabit al-Zubayri narrated, from his father, from Hanzalah ibn Qays, from Abd Allah ibn 'Amir ibn Kurayz - I deem from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"14913","Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14874 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated - they said: Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather Furat, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: 'Utbah ibn Farqad wrote to Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr seeking a ruling on the grandfather; he wrote: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were taking a close friend of my ummah besides my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as close friend; but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave. And Abu Bakr used to give him the station of a father."
"14914","Ahnaf Abu Furat, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14875 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated, he said: Malik ibn Su'ayr ibn al-Khums narrated, he said: Furat ibn Ahnaf narrated, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Hajj: Which land is most sacred? It was said: Makkah. He said: Which month is most sacred? It was said: Dhu al-Hijjah. He said: Which day is most sacred? He said: The day of sacrifice, the day of the Greater Hajj. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours."
"14915","Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14876 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, he said: Isra'il narrated, from Thuwayr, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: This is the day of 'Ashura, so fast it, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting it."
"14916","Abd Allah ibn Sharik al-'Amiri, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14877 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani narrated. And Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated - they said: Sharik narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Sharik al-'Amiri, he said: I asked Ibn 'Umar, Ibn 'Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr about 'umrah before Hajj? They said: The sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): you arrive, circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then release; even if that is a day before 'Arafah. Then you enter ihram for Hajj - so you have joined an 'umrah and a Hajj."
"14917","Nusayr ibn Dhu'luq, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14878 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Nusayr ibn Dhu'luq, that Ibn al-Zubayr saw the people wiping the Maqam, and forbade them, saying: You were not commanded to wipe; you were only commanded to pray."
"14918","14879 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated, he said: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, he said: Sharik narrated, from Nusayr ibn Dhu'luq, he said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr circumambulating with a burtulah upon him."
"14919","Abu 'Awn Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14880 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated, he said: Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated, from Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal, from Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: The people used to rely upon one another for provisions, so Allah ordered them to take provisions, saying: And take provisions, for the best provision is piety."
"14920","Zur'ah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14881 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated, he said: 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated, he said: al-'Ala ibn Salih narrated, he said: Zur'ah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: Aligning the feet, and placing hand upon hand in prayer, is of the sunnah."
"14921","'Amir al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14882 - Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from 'Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, while circumambulating the Ka'bah, saying: By the Lord of this building! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) surely cursed al-Hakam and his offspring!"
"14922","14883 - Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, he said: Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that he said while upon the pulpit: By the Lord of this Sacred House and Sacred Land! Al-Hakam ibn Abi al-'As and his offspring are cursed upon the tongue of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14923","14884 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated, he said: Ibn Fudayl narrated, from Ibn Shubrumah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) curse al-Hakam and his offspring."
"14924","Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14885 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Sa'iqah narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one consulted is trusted."
"14925","Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14886 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated, he said: 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib narrated, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: When there was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You are to die, and they are to die; then you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute - al-Zubayr said: Will what was between us in this world be repeated upon us? He said: Yes - it shall surely be repeated upon you until every rightful one is given his right. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah! The matter is grave!"
"14926","14887 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: When was revealed: Then you shall surely be asked that day of bliss - al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam said: O Messenger of Allah, what bliss shall we be asked of? They are but the two blacks: water and dates? He said: It shall indeed be."
"14927","Sulayman ibn 'Atiq, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14888 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn 'Ubayd al-Tustari narrated, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Sulayman ibn 'Atiq, he heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among mosques."
"14928","Sulayman ibn Ziyad, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14889 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj al-'Askari narrated, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Sulayman ibn Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: We ate roast with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while we were in the mosque; the prayer was established, and we did no more than wipe with pebbles."
"14929","Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Zubayr: 14890 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Kharraz al-Razi narrated, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not of us who raises arms against us."
"14930","Abu al-Zubayr Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Makki, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14891 - Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated, he said: Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: After prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: There is no god but Allah; we worship none but Him; Possessor of blessing, bounty, and good praise; there is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion though the disbelievers dislike."
"14931","14892 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi al-Ramli and Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr narrated, they said: Adam narrated, he said: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: At the end of his prayer before rising, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is dominion and His is praise, and He is over all things Capable; there is no might and no power except through Allah; we worship none but Him; His is blessing, His is bounty, His is good praise; there is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion."
"14932","14893 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated, he said: Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated, he said: Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Muhammad ibn Muslim Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: After prayer, when he gave salam before rising, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say, raising his voice with that: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is dominion and His is praise, and He is over all things Capable; there is no might and no power except through Allah; we worship none but Him; His is blessing, His is bounty, His is good praise; there is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion though the disbelievers dislike."
"14933","14894 - 'Umar ibn al-'Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated, he said: My father narrated, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated, he said: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim informed us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of the hadith of Hafs ibn Maysarah from Musa ibn 'Uqbah."
"14934","14895 - al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas al-Razi narrated, he said: Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated, he said: Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm, Nafi' not mentioned, and it is the correct."
"14935","Abu Dhubyan Khalifah ibn Ka'b, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: 14896 - Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Ja'far ibn Maymun al-Basri, he said: Khalifah ibn Ka'b narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr addressed us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world shall not wear it in the Hereafter."
"14936","14897 - Thabit al-Bunani from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, he said: Fitr ibn Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr addressed us and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"14937","14898 - Abd al-Aziz ibn Asid from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Asid, he said: A man said to Ibn al-Zubayr: Give us a fatwa about nabidh made in earthen jars, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding nabidh of the earthen jar."
"14938","14899 - Abu Amir Salim ibn Amir from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sulaym ibn Amir, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prescribed prayer except that before it are two rak'ahs."
"14939","14900 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, he said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ajlan, from Sulaym ibn Amir, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr recite this verse: {They said: two magicians supporting each other}."
"14940","14901 - Suhayl ibn Dhakwan from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr delivering a sermon, and he said: Ibn Abbas permits mut'ah while it is unlawful by Allah and His Messenger."
"14941","14902 - Wahb ibn Kaysan from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi, he said: Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr led us in prayer on the day of Eid, then he delivered the sermon after the prayer, then he said: Every practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been changed by so-and-so, even the prayer."
"14942","14903 - Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Najiyah, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, he said: Abd Allah ibn Utbah wrote to Ibn al-Zubayr - and he had appointed him over Iraq - asking him about the grandfather, so he wrote to him: The one about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to take a close friend I would have taken him as a close friend - made the grandfather a father who takes possession of the property."
"14943","14904 - Subay' al-Saluli from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Subay' al-Saluli, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Before the Hour there will be thirty liars, among them al-Aswad al-Ansi, the man of San'a, and the man of Yamamah."
"14944","14905 - Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Subay' al-Saluli, from Ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14945","14906 - Abu al-Ward from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ward say: I heard Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the tashahhud: In the name of Allah and by Allah, best of names; greetings belong to Allah, the good and pure prayers; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, and the Hour is coming, there is no doubt in it; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; O Allah, forgive me and guide me. This is in the first two rak'ahs."
"14946","14907 - Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami from Ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Attar, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, he said: I saw Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, and he saw a man raising his hands supplicating before finishing his prayer, and when he finished it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands until he finished his prayer."
"14947","14908 - Unnamed men from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr: Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Abu Habib, from a man of the people of Hijaz, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"14948","14909 - Narrated to us Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, he said: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Sinan Abu Habib, from a man who narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"14949","14910 - What Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq narrated, may Allah be pleased with them both: Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham the muezzin narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Haytham Abu Muhammad al-Sulami, from Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Ansari, from al-Jahm ibn Uthman ibn Abi Jahmah, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim man reaches fifty years, Allah turns away from him three kinds of affliction: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo; when he reaches sixty years, Allah grants him return to Him; when he reaches seventy years, his evil deeds are erased and his good deeds are written; when he reaches ninety years, Allah forgives him his sins, past and future, and he becomes Allah's captive on earth, and he intercedes for the people of his household."
"14950","14911 - Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, brother of Umm Salamah on her father's side, whose mother was Atikah bint Abd al-Muttalib, aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he accepted Islam on the day of the conquest, met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the road and accepted Islam, and was martyred on the day of Ta'if with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Narrated to us al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; and narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah informed me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, wrapped in it, crossing its two ends."
"14951","14912 - Narrated to us Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, he said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Makhzumi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of Umm Salamah praying in a single garment, crossing its two ends."
"14952","14913 - What Abd Allah ibn Harithah ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari narrated: Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us; and narrated to us Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Harithah ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Harithah, he said: When Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf al-Jumahi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With whom did you stay, O Abu Wahb? He said: I stayed with al-Abbas. He said: You stayed with the one of Quraysh who loves Quraysh most."
"14953","14914 - Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari, and he is the one whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Sufyan al-Hudhali, and he killed him. What Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari narrated; Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; and narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja' al-Ghudani and Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to him, he said: A hadith reached me from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I had not heard it from him, so I feared he would die or I would die before I heard it, so I bought a camel, saddled it, then traveled on it for a month until I came to Syria, and I came to Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari, and I stood and asked permission, and I said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah; so he came out to me and embraced me and I embraced him. He said: I said: A hadith reached me that you heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wrongs, and I feared you would die or I would die before I heard it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah will gather the servants - and he gestured with his hand toward Syria - naked, barefoot, uncircumcised, with nothing - he said: I said: What is with nothing? He said: They have nothing with them - then a caller will call in a voice heard by the distant as the near hear it: I am the King, the Recompenser; it is not fitting for anyone of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while anyone of the people of Hell seeks him for a wrong, nor for anyone of the people of Hell to enter Hell while anyone of the people of Paradise seeks him for a wrong, even a slap. He said: I said: And how, when we come naked, uncircumcised, with nothing? He said: By good deeds and evil deeds."
"14954","14915 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi', from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will deal with Sufyan al-Hudhali for me? He satirizes me, reviles me, and harms me?! So I said to him: I will, O Messenger of Allah, send me to him. So he sent him to him, and when he came to him at night he entered his house and called: Where is Sufyan? One of his household looked out at him and said: What do you want? He said: I want Sufyan, so tell him to look out at me; so Sufyan looked out at him and said: What do you want? He said: I want you to come down to me, for I have a coat of mail I want to show you. He said: Where is it? He said: Here it is, so come down to me in your cloak and come out with me so I may show it to you; so he came out with him, then he drew his sword and struck him until he grew cold, then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the gathering and informed him that he had killed him, and with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a staff he leaned upon, so he handed it to him and said: Lean upon this, for those who lean upon staffs on the Day of Resurrection are few; and it remained with him until he died, and it was buried with him."
"14955","14916 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli, he said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, that his father narrated to him, from his mother, the daughter of Abd Allah ibn Unays, that she narrated to him from Abd Allah ibn Unays: that the group whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Huqayq to kill him were: Abd Allah ibn Atik, Abd Allah ibn Unays, Abu Qatadah and an ally of theirs, and a man of the Ansar, and they came to Khaybar at night. So we went to their doors and locked them from outside. The wife of Ibn Abi al-Huqayq said: This is surely the voice of Abd Allah ibn Atik. He said: Open. So she opened, and I entered, I and Abd Allah ibn Atik. Abd Allah said: She is yours. So I went to strike her with the sword, then I remembered the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against killing women and children, so I held back from her. Ali ibn al-Madini said: This is Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari, and he is not al-Juhani; this is Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari, from whom Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated."
"14956","14917 - Narrated to us Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Muqbil al-Basri, he said: Ishaq ibn Wahb al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Huwaysah, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari, he said: al-Yastatir ibn Rizam the Jew struck my face with a palm-branch implement of shawhat wood, and wounded me with a wound laying bare the bone, or reaching the brain; so I brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he uncovered it and spat upon it, and nothing of it ever harmed me after."
"14957","14918 - Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi from Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Ansari: Narrated to us Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: Abd Allah ibn Unays said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Who will deal with Khalid ibn Nubayh for me? A man of Hudhayl, and he was that day at Arafah. Abd Allah said: So I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me. So he said: If you saw him you would fear him. So I said: By the One who honored you, I have never feared anything at all. So I went out until I met him at the mountains of Arafah before the sun set, and I met him and I was seized with fear of him, and I knew when I was seized with fear of him what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said. So he said: Who is the man? So I said: One seeking a need; is there lodging? He said: Yes, so join me. He said: So I went out in his tracks, and I prayed Asr as two light rak'ahs, then I went out, fearing he would see me, then I caught up with him and struck him with the sword, then I covered myself with the mountain and lay in ambush, until when the people departed I came out, until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and informed him of the news. Muhammad ibn Ka'b said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a short staff and said: Lean upon this until you meet me with it on the Day of Resurrection, and the fewest of people that day will be those who lean upon staffs. Muhammad ibn Ka'b said: When Abd Allah ibn Unays died he ordered that it be placed upon his belly, and he was shrouded over it, and it was buried with him."
"14958","14919 - Abd Allah ibn Unays ibn Haram al-Juhani, who used to reside in Madinah, an ally of Banu Nabi ibn Amr ibn Sawwad; a participant at Aqabah. Isa ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays from his father: Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Isa ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him regarding the night of the twenty-third."
"14959","14920 - Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Abd al-A'la al-Bawsi and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Barrah al-San'anis, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Isa ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to a waterskin and fold its mouth, then drink while standing."
"14960","14921 - Damrah ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays from his father: Narrated to us Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir al-Naji narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, he said: I asked Damrah ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays about the Night of Decree, so he said: I heard my father report from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Seek it on the night of the twenty-third."
"14961","14922 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: I said to Damrah ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to your father about the Night of Decree? He said: My father was a man of the desert, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, command me a night in which I come down, he said: Come down on the night of the twenty-third. He said: When he turned away, he said: Seek it in the last ten."
"14962","14923 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed me, from Ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am at al-Rahilah, and I, by the praise of Allah, pray there, so command me a night on which I come down to this mosque and pray in it. He said: Come down on the night of the twenty-third."
"14963","14924 - Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays, from his father, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in our desert, and I, by the praise of Allah, pray there, so command me a night of this month on which I come down to the mosque and pray in it. So he said: Come down on the night of the twenty-third and pray it, and if you wish to complete to the end of the month, do so, and if you wish to return to your family by night, do so."
"14964","14925 - Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays from his father: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to us, he said: Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to me, from his father, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me which night the Night of Decree is sought in? So he said: Were it not that people would abandon prayer except that night, I would have informed you; but seek it on the twenty-third of the month."
"14965","14926 - Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays from his father: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, that Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri informed him, that Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik al-Ansari and Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays informed him, that Abd Allah ibn Unays informed them, that a group of the Ansar said: Which man shall we send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Abd Allah said: So I said: I will. They said: Go and ask him for us: When is the Night of Decree? So I went out until I arrived at sunset near one of the dwellings of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to pray Maghrib, and he prayed; then he went out, and I went out with him until he entered his house, I with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for his fast-breaking meal. Abd Allah ibn Unays said: And I found myself watching the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of the scantiness of his food; then when he finished he called for his sandals, then he said: I think you have a need? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so and so-and-so sent me to you asking you: When is the Night of Decree? He said: Tonight - and that night was the night of the twenty-second of Ramadan - then he said: Which night is it? I said: The night of the twenty-second. He said: No, rather the coming night; the night of the twenty-third."
"14966","14927 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: We used to discuss in Ramadan, and our people said: It is hard upon us to come down with our dependents and our women, and we fear waste befalling them if we come down and leave them, and we dislike missing this night; would you send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mention this to him and ask him to command us a night on which we come down?! Abd Allah said: So they sent me, and I was the youngest of them in speech; so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and asked him to command us a night on which we come down. So he said: Come down on the night of the twenty-third. And Abd Allah used to come down that night, and when morning came he returned."
"14967","14928 - Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Darrab al-Asbahani, he said: Yahya ibn Ward ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Damrah ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b, that they heard Abd Allah ibn Unays say: I sat in the gathering of Banu Salimah, I being the youngest of them, on the morning of the twenty-first of Ramadan, and they said: Who will ask for us the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When is the Night of Decree? So I said: I will. So I went until I arrived at Maghrib on the night of the twenty-second, and I prayed the prayer with him, then I stood for him at his door until he passed by me, and he admitted me into his house, and he called for supper for me and said to me: Eat supper; and I found myself holding back from it because of its scantiness. Then he called for his sandals and stood, and said: It is as if you have a need? I said: Yes, men of Banu Salimah sent me to you asking you: When is the Night of Decree? So he said: What night of the month is it? So I said: Twenty-two. So he said: It is tonight. Then he reconsidered and said: Or the next, or the next."
"14968","14929 - The daughter of Abd Allah ibn Unays from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi, he said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Jari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to me, from his father, from Khalidah bint Abd Allah ibn Unays, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Night of Decree. So he said: I saw myself prostrating in water and mud. So I said: Make clear to me when I should seek it. So he said: Seek it in the last half. I said: In which of the last half? He said: On the twenty-third."
"14969","14930 - Atiyyah ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays from his father: Narrated to us Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to me, from his father Bilal ibn Abd Allah, from Atiyyah ibn Abd Allah, from his father Abd Allah ibn Unays, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Night of Decree. So he said: I saw it and then I was made to forget it; so seek it in the last half. Then he returned and asked him, and he said: On the twenty-third passing of the month. Abd al-Aziz said: My mother informed me that Abd Allah ibn Unays used to keep alive the night of the sixteenth to the night of the twenty-third."
"14970","14931 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, so I stood at his left; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me and placed me at his right, and upon me was a torn garment that did not cover me, so whenever I prostrated I held it with my hand fearing my private parts would be uncovered, and behind me were women. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he called for a garment for me and clothed me with it, and said: Use this worn-out one of yours for your work. This Abu al-Hasan from whom Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated is Muhajir; the Abu al-Hasan from whom Shu'bah narrated is Kufan; and Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman is Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, brother of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla."
"14971","14932 - Abu Umamah ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Yahya and Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi, from Abu Umamah al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Among the gravest of major sins are: association with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the engulfing oath; and no swearer swears by Allah a binding oath in which he inserts even the like of a gnat's wing except it becomes a black spot in his heart until the Day of Resurrection."
"14972","14933 - Narrated to us Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Khalid showed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Umamah, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gravest of major sins are: association with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the engulfing oath; and by the One in whose hand is my soul, no one swears - even over the like of a gnat's wing - except it becomes a black spot in his heart until the Day of Resurrection."
"14973","14934 - Al-Hasan ibn Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays from his grandfather: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yazid, my uncle, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Unays: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him on a detachment alone."
"14974","14935 - Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas al-Misri, he said: my father narrated to us; and narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab al-Ansari narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to him: that he and Umar ibn al-Khattab one day discussed charity, so Umar said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention misappropriation of charity: whoever misappropriates from it a camel or a sheep will be brought carrying it on the Day of Resurrection? Abd Allah ibn Unays said: Yes."
"14975","14936 - Busr ibn Sa'id from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, he said: Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown the Night of Decree and then I was made to forget it, and I see myself prostrating in water and mud. Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in water and mud on the morning of the twenty-third."
"14976","14937 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14977","14938 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw myself on the Night of Decree prostrating in water and mud. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer on the night of the twenty-third, and I saw him prostrating in water and mud."
"14978","14939 - Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Khubayb from Abd Allah ibn Unays: Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, he said: Abu Salih Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Mu'adh ibn Abd Allah ibn Khubayb, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Khubayb, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about the Night of Decree. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seek it tonight - and that night was the night of the twenty-third - so a man said: O Messenger of Allah, then it is the beginning of eight? He said: Rather the beginning of seven, for the month does not complete."
"14979","14940 - Abd Allah ibn Salam, may Allah be pleased with him: Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from the nephew of Abd Allah ibn Salam, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: My name in the pre-Islamic age was so-and-so, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abd Allah."
"14980","14941 - What Abd Allah ibn Salam narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu Hurayrah from Abd Allah ibn Salam, may Allah be pleased with them both: Narrated to us Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq showed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sits waiting for prayer is in prayer."
"14981","14942 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever awaits the prayer is in prayer until he prays."
"14982","14943 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, and Abdan ibn Ahmad, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever awaits the prayer is in prayer until he prays."
"14983","14944 - Narrated to us Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and narrated to us Bakr ibn Sahl, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, both from Malik, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever awaits the prayer is in prayer."
"14984","14945 - Narrated to us Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi, he said: Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Abu Hurayrah used to narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim coincides with while he is in prayer asking Allah for good except He gives it to him; Abu Hurayrah would make it seem brief with his hand. When Abu Hurayrah died, I said: If only I came to Abu Sa'id and asked him? So I came to him and asked him, then I went out from him and entered upon Abd Allah ibn Salam and asked him, so he said: Allah created Adam on Friday, and took his soul on Friday, and on it the Hour will come, and it is the last hour. So I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: in prayer, yet it is not a time of prayer? So he said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one awaiting prayer is in prayer? I said: Yes. He said: Then by Allah, it is it."
"14985","14946 - Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib, he said: Salm ibn Ibrahim al-Warraq narrated to us; and narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Sinan Abu Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us - they said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib claimed that Abd Allah ibn Salam passed through the market carrying a bundle of firewood, so it was said to him: What carries you to this when Allah has sufficed you from this? He said: I wanted to repel pride; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None shall enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard seed of pride."
"14986","14947 - Anas ibn Malik from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while Abd Allah ibn Salam was among his date-palms, so Abd Allah ibn Salam came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I will ask you about things which none knows but a prophet; if you inform me of them I will believe in you... the hadith."
"14987","14948 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Iqal al-Harrani, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salam said: O Messenger of Allah, I have accepted Islam, and I love to ask you about things. So he said: Ask whatever occurs to you. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the child's resemblance to its mother, when the fluid is only from the man? So he said: The fluid of the man is white and thick, and the fluid of the woman is red and thin; so whichever of them overcomes its companion, the resemblance belongs to it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the food of the people of Paradise in Paradise when they enter it? He said: The extra lobe of the liver of a whale. I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the signs of the Hour? He said: A fire will come out from the east and drive the people to their gathering place. So he said: I bear witness that you are a prophet."
"14988","14949 - Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil al-Muzani from Abd Allah ibn Salam: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Ma'qil, from Abd Allah ibn Salam, that he said when the people rose in the affair of Uthman: O people, do not kill this old man but seek satisfaction from him, for no community will kill its prophet and its affair be set right until seventy thousand of them have blood shed, and no community will kill its caliph and its affair be set right until forty thousand of them have blood shed. But they did not consider what he said and killed him. Then he sat waiting for Ali on the road and said: Where do you intend? He said: I intend the land of Iraq. And he said: Do not come to Iraq, but keep to the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So some of the companions of Ali leapt at him and were about to attack him, so Ali said: Leave him, for he is a man of us, the people of the house. When Ali was killed, Ibn Salam said to Ibn Ma'qil: This is the head of the forty, and at its head there will be a reconciliation; and no community will kill its prophet but seventy thousand are killed for him, and no community will kill its caliph but forty thousand are killed for him."
"14989","14950 - Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam from his father: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, he said: Ammar ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, from his father, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my community in its early morning."
"14990","14951 - Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, he said: Ammar ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, from his father, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deception."
"14991","14952 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us; and narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, he said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us; and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki and Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar, they said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; and narrated to us Ahmad ibn Rushdin al-Misri, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us - they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, that Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, from Awn ibn Abd Allah, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the people were heard saying: Which deed is best, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith in Allah and His Messenger, striving in His path, and an accepted pilgrimage. Then he heard a call in the valley saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I bear witness, and I bear witness; none bears them except he is cleared of association. And the wording is that of the hadith of Ahmad ibn Salih."
"14992","14953 - Narrated to us Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among some of his Companions when Uthman ibn Affan approached with a mount bearing two sacks, holding the halter of his camel wrapped round him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is in the two sacks? He said: Flour, ghee, and honey. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Make it kneel. So he made it kneel. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a pot and placed in it some of that flour, ghee, and honey, then mixed it, then ate, then said to his Companions: Eat; this is what the Persians call khabis."
"14993","14954 - Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, he said: my father narrated to us; and narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar al-Baghdadi, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: When Allah intended the guidance of Zayd ibn Sa'nah, Zayd ibn Sa'nah said: There is no sign of prophethood except I recognized it in the face of Muhammad when I looked at him, except two I had not experienced in him: his forbearance precedes his anger, and the severity of anger against him only increases him in forbearance. So I was gentle with him until I mixed with him, that I might know his forbearance from his anger. Zayd ibn Sa'nah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day from the chambers, with him Ali ibn Abi Talib, and a man on his mount like a Bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, near me is the village of Banu so-and-so; they have accepted Islam and entered into Islam, and I had told them if they accepted Islam provision would come to them abundantly, but a year of drought, hardship, and lack of rain has struck them, and I fear - O Messenger of Allah - they will leave Islam out of desire, as they entered it out of desire; so if you see fit to send them something to help them with, do so. He looked at a man beside him - I think it was Ali - who said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing of it remains. Zayd ibn Sa'nah said: So I drew near to him and said: O Muhammad, will you sell me known dates in the garden of Banu so-and-so until such-and-such a term? He said: No, O Jew, but I will sell you known dates until such-and-such a term, and we shall not name the garden of Banu so-and-so. I said: Yes. So he traded with me, and I loosened my purse and gave him eighty mithqals of gold for known dates until such-and-such a term, and he gave it to the man and said: Deal justly with them and help them with it. Zayd ibn Sa'nah said: Two or three days before the term fell due, the Messenger of Allah came out, with him Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman among a group of his Companions; when he had prayed over a funeral and drawn near a wall to sit, I came to him and seized the front of his shirt and cloak, and looked at him with a stern face, and said to him: Will you not pay me my due, O Muhammad? By Allah, I never knew you - Banu Abd al-Muttalib - but delayers; and I had knowledge through mixing with you. And I looked at Umar, and his eyes were turning in his face like a revolving orbit, then he cast his glance at me and said: O enemy of Allah, do you say to the Messenger of Allah what I hear, and do to him what I see? By the One who sent him with the truth, were it not that I fear missing him, I would have struck your head with my sword. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking at Umar with calm and composure, and smiled, then said: O Umar, he and I needed other than this: that you command me good performance, and command him good exaction. Go with him, O Umar, and give him his due, and add twenty sa's of dates in place of your frightening him. Zayd said: So Umar went with me and gave me my due and added twenty sa's of dates. So I said: What is this addition, O Umar? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to add to you in place of my frightening you. He said: And do you know me, O Umar? He said: No. What moved you to do to the Messenger of Allah what you did and say to him what you said? I said: O Umar, there was no sign of prophethood except I recognized it in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I looked at him, except two I had not experienced in him: his forbearance precedes his anger, and the severity of anger against him only increases him in forbearance; and I have tested them both. So I call you to witness, O Umar, that I am pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as prophet; and I call you to witness that half my wealth - for I am the wealthiest of them in wealth - is charity upon the community of Muhammad. Umar said: Or upon some of them, for you cannot encompass them. I said: Or upon some of them. So Umar and Zayd returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Zayd said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And he believed in him, affirmed him, followed him, witnessed many battles with him, then died in the expedition of Tabuk, advancing, not retreating. May Allah have mercy on Zayd."
"14994","14955 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, he said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, he said: al-Walid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father: that Abd Allah ibn Salam said to the rabbis of the Jews: I make a covenant at the mosque of our father Ibrahim and Isma'il. So he set out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Makkah, and he met them when they had turned from the pilgrimage, and he found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, the people around him, so he stood with the people. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him he said: Are you Abd Allah ibn Salam? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Come near. So I drew near to him. He said: I adjure you by Allah, O Abd Allah ibn Salam, do you not find me in the Torah as the Messenger of Allah? So I said to him: Describe our Lord. He said: So Gabriel, peace be upon him, came until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: {Say: He is Allah, One; Allah, the Eternal; He neither begets nor is born; and there is none like unto Him}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it to us. Ibn Salam said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that you are the Messenger of Allah. Then Ibn Salam departed to Madinah and concealed his Islam. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emigrated and came to Madinah, I being atop a palm of mine cutting its dates, I heard a stir in Madinah and said: What is this? They said: This is the Messenger of Allah arrived. So I threw myself from the top of the palm, then I came hurrying until I came to him, and I greeted him, then I returned. Then my mother said: May Allah be with you; by Allah, if it were Musa ibn Imran, peace be upon him, your lot would not be to throw yourself from the top of the palm. So I said: By Allah, I am more joyful at the coming of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than at Musa ibn Imran when he was sent."
"14995","14956 - Narrated to us Hajjaj ibn Imran al-Sadusi, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on Friday and said: What is upon any of you if he took two garments for his Friday, besides the two garments of his work?"
"14996","14957 - Narrated to us al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, are we better or those after us? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of them had the like of Uhud in gold and spent it in the path of Allah, it would not reach the mudd of one of you nor half of it."
"14997","14958 - Narrated to us Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath al-Kufi, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us; and narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali, Uqbah ibn Mukram, and Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, they said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Utbah ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: We would be with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he spoke he raised his head to the sky."
"14998","14959 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no prayer for one who turns away."
"14999","14960 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, he said: Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from al-Salt ibn Tarif, from a man, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no prayer for one who turns away."
"15000","14961 - Narrated to us Abdan ibn Ahmad, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Ghiyath ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have read the Qur'an, the Torah, and the Gospel. He said: Read with this one night, and with this one night."
